1
00:00:01,173 --> 00:00:04,376
(Wonder Dogs are currently
at four wins and two losses.)

2
00:00:05,263 --> 00:00:07,632
The final match,
with their survival already secured.

3
00:00:07,966 --> 00:00:10,268
The last match is being held
at their home stadium.

4
00:00:10,268 --> 00:00:12,971
With their fans cheering for them.

5
00:00:14,205 --> 00:00:18,475
(From a celebration cheering squad
to prizes)

6
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:22,124
Everyone, please hold up
your cheering signs!

7
00:00:22,305 --> 00:00:24,640
"Send Pyo Seung Ju to the national team."

8
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:28,544
"Let's win this
before Coach Kim swears off."

9
00:00:30,401 --> 00:00:32,012
(The highlight of the live match)

10
00:00:32,012 --> 00:00:33,581
Before we start the match,

11
00:00:33,582 --> 00:00:36,518
we have prepared
a special stage to celebrate.

12
00:00:36,952 --> 00:00:39,254
The refreshing idol group
symbolizing youth.

13
00:00:39,254 --> 00:00:41,156
Please welcome TWS!

14
00:00:44,827 --> 00:00:46,528
They're so good-looking.

15
00:00:46,528 --> 00:00:47,729
Their faces are so small!

16
00:00:47,729 --> 00:00:48,930
Their proportions are amazing.

17
00:00:49,031 --> 00:00:50,666
- Their faces are just...
- I know.

18
00:00:50,666 --> 00:00:53,435
They are in the same agency as us.

19
00:00:55,357 --> 00:00:59,302
("Plot twist" by TWS)

20
00:01:04,687 --> 00:01:08,524
(Three, two, one)

21
00:01:08,872 --> 00:01:10,807
(First encounters are...)

22
00:01:10,808 --> 00:01:11,293
(Always)
(So)

23
00:01:11,897 --> 00:01:12,528
(Hard)

24
00:01:13,136 --> 00:01:16,439
(The 54 days of this volleyball adventure
have never gone according to plan.)

25
00:01:16,866 --> 00:01:21,137
(Their journey to survive
and face their fans was not an easy one.)

26
00:01:21,671 --> 00:01:25,041
(And now, it's time for their last match.)

27
00:01:26,275 --> 00:01:27,176
(Screaming)

28
00:01:29,445 --> 00:01:32,348
- Go, Pilseung Wonder Dogs!
- Go, Wonder Dogs!

29
00:01:32,348 --> 00:01:34,250
(Go, Wonder Dogs!)

30
00:01:36,624 --> 00:01:39,594
This is their first live match
with crowds.

31
00:01:40,094 --> 00:01:42,530
- And the last match of Wonder Dogs.
- That is right.

32
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:44,999
The players might find
today's match exciting,

33
00:01:45,133 --> 00:01:47,235
or they could be feeling nervous.

34
00:01:47,702 --> 00:01:50,171
The last opponent for Wonder Dogs.

35
00:01:50,401 --> 00:01:52,707
Pink Spiders, the team
with the most wins in the V-League.

36
00:01:52,707 --> 00:01:53,708
Correct.

37
00:01:53,876 --> 00:01:56,510
They won the overall championship
last season.

38
00:01:56,511 --> 00:01:59,147
Both the regular season
and the championship finals.

39
00:01:59,147 --> 00:02:02,484
They have shown everyone that
they are the strongest team alive.

40
00:02:02,736 --> 00:02:05,604
Their head coach,
Yoshihara Tomoko, is not here today.

41
00:02:05,604 --> 00:02:07,806
Coach Kim Dae Kyung is going
to oversee the game today.

42
00:02:07,806 --> 00:02:11,843
Coach Kim Dae Kyung
and Coach Kim Yeon Koung...

43
00:02:11,844 --> 00:02:13,846
- go way back, actually.
- Right.

44
00:02:14,113 --> 00:02:17,650
I'm sure you know everything
you need to know about Coach Yeon Koung.

45
00:02:17,990 --> 00:02:21,782
Mostly about what kind
of tactics she might be pulling out...

46
00:02:21,783 --> 00:02:24,423
- Mostly?
- or the players' traits.

47
00:02:24,423 --> 00:02:27,026
She was one of the key players
in the last championship,

48
00:02:27,026 --> 00:02:30,963
and I'm guessing her tactics
mostly come from her play style.

49
00:02:31,864 --> 00:02:35,501
Coach Kim Dae Kyung has
assembled the team for today.

50
00:02:35,501 --> 00:02:38,504
There are a lot of first-team players,

51
00:02:38,504 --> 00:02:40,539
- That is right.
- and national team players too.

52
00:02:40,539 --> 00:02:44,597
Moon Ji Yun and Jeong Yun Ju were
on the national team,

53
00:02:44,597 --> 00:02:46,866
and they have joined the team
quite recently.

54
00:02:46,867 --> 00:02:49,355
The Wonder Dogs are going
against a very strong team,

55
00:02:49,356 --> 00:02:52,338
and I cannot wait to see
what kind of game they will play today.

56
00:02:53,442 --> 00:02:55,269
(A match against a team
that knows us well)

57
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:57,946
I belong to the Pink Spiders
as an adviser,

58
00:02:58,553 --> 00:03:00,021
but I have no intention
of going easy on them.

59
00:03:01,092 --> 00:03:04,897
I'm going to try my best to defeat them.

60
00:03:05,964 --> 00:03:08,566
Here is the starting lineup
for both teams.

61
00:03:08,566 --> 00:03:10,501
First, the Pilseung Wonder Dogs.

62
00:03:10,502 --> 00:03:12,371
Setter Lee Na Yeon in Zone One.

63
00:03:12,570 --> 00:03:14,205
Outside hitter Pyo Seung Ju.

64
00:03:14,305 --> 00:03:16,007
Middle blocker Moon Myoung Hwa.

65
00:03:16,007 --> 00:03:17,842
Opposite spiker Han Song Hee.

66
00:03:17,842 --> 00:03:19,711
Outside hitter Enkhsoyol.

67
00:03:19,711 --> 00:03:21,513
Middle blocker Kim Hyeon Jeong.

68
00:03:21,913 --> 00:03:23,715
(Libero Koo Hye In)

69
00:03:23,715 --> 00:03:25,650
And going against them, the Pink Spiders.

70
00:03:25,650 --> 00:03:28,186
Starting from Zone One,
Choi Eun Ji, the outside hitter.

71
00:03:28,186 --> 00:03:29,988
Opposite spiker Moon Ji Yun.

72
00:03:29,988 --> 00:03:31,323
Middle blocker Lim Hye Rim.

73
00:03:31,589 --> 00:03:33,291
Outside hitter Kim Da Eun.

74
00:03:33,558 --> 00:03:35,093
Middle blocker Pyeon Ji Su.

75
00:03:35,193 --> 00:03:36,995
Setter Kim Da Sol.

76
00:03:37,696 --> 00:03:39,864
(Libero Do Su Been)

77
00:03:40,231 --> 00:03:42,733
Let's stay focused in the beginning.

78
00:03:42,734 --> 00:03:45,170
Receive it, set it, and spike it well.

79
00:03:45,170 --> 00:03:47,272
Stick to the basics
and cover for each other.

80
00:03:47,806 --> 00:03:50,508
This is our last game. Let's have fun.

81
00:03:50,508 --> 00:03:52,176
- One, two, three. Let's go!
- Let's go!

82
00:03:52,310 --> 00:03:54,379
- Let's go, Wonder Dogs!
- Let's go!

83
00:03:54,379 --> 00:03:56,214
- Let's do this!
- Let's go!

84
00:03:56,215 --> 00:03:57,833
(Their last opponent, the pro champion.)

85
00:03:58,576 --> 00:04:01,151
(Wonder Dogs running
towards the end with no regrets)

86
00:04:01,152 --> 00:04:02,854
Relax, guys.

87
00:04:06,385 --> 00:04:08,793
Remember to set it up high.

88
00:04:08,793 --> 00:04:10,662
Let's go, guys.

89
00:04:10,662 --> 00:04:12,063
Stay focused.

90
00:04:12,063 --> 00:04:14,132
(Wonder Dogs versus Pink Spiders)

91
00:04:14,399 --> 00:04:17,268
Everything is ready for this match.

92
00:04:17,569 --> 00:04:19,938
With Eun Ji from the Pink Spiders serving,

93
00:04:20,271 --> 00:04:22,340
The Wonder Dogs' last match
is starting now.

94
00:04:22,841 --> 00:04:24,142
Set one gets underway.

95
00:04:24,142 --> 00:04:25,877
Na Yeon, go C!

96
00:04:26,211 --> 00:04:27,145
Under-toss.

97
00:04:27,945 --> 00:04:29,214
Song Hee sprints to the ball.

98
00:04:29,214 --> 00:04:30,515
(Small giant is coming.)

99
00:04:30,515 --> 00:04:32,017
(Oh, no.)

100
00:04:32,817 --> 00:04:34,685
It's blocked.

101
00:04:34,986 --> 00:04:36,421
Nice.

102
00:04:37,489 --> 00:04:38,723
Nice block.

103
00:04:39,283 --> 00:04:40,751
(First set, Pink Spiders 1: Wonder Dogs 0)

104
00:04:43,326 --> 00:04:44,627
Sorry, my bad.

105
00:04:45,075 --> 00:04:46,008
It's okay.

106
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:48,137
Song Hee, it's okay.

107
00:04:48,565 --> 00:04:50,072
Hit it deep.

108
00:04:50,073 --> 00:04:51,374
Okay, Coach.

109
00:04:53,017 --> 00:04:57,421
I really hoped
we could have won the first point.

110
00:04:57,421 --> 00:04:59,356
But that was just one point.

111
00:04:59,907 --> 00:05:02,154
(Eun Ji serving again)

112
00:05:02,627 --> 00:05:04,895
Let's hear the applause.

113
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,637
(Wonder Dogs home crowd)

114
00:05:07,866 --> 00:05:10,367
Everyone, let's hear your cheer.
Wonder Dogs.

115
00:05:10,367 --> 00:05:11,468
- Go, Wonder Dogs!
- Go, Wonder Dogs!

116
00:05:11,468 --> 00:05:12,602
Wonder Dogs.

117
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:13,704
- Go, Wonder Dogs!
- Go, Wonder Dogs!

118
00:05:13,704 --> 00:05:16,373
- One more time. Wonder Dogs.
- Go, Wonder Dogs!

119
00:05:16,373 --> 00:05:18,575
- Wonder Dogs.
- Go, Wonder Dogs!

120
00:05:18,575 --> 00:05:20,610
Let's keep this energy.

121
00:05:24,782 --> 00:05:26,684
A serving error. Net violation.

122
00:05:27,543 --> 00:05:30,446
(First set, Pink Spiders 1: Wonder Dogs 1)

123
00:05:31,188 --> 00:05:32,122
Nice.

124
00:05:32,890 --> 00:05:33,791
Nice.

125
00:05:34,725 --> 00:05:35,726
Nice.

126
00:05:35,726 --> 00:05:38,056
(Putting pressure on the away team)

127
00:05:39,329 --> 00:05:41,631
Guys, let's try to have some fun.

128
00:05:41,932 --> 00:05:42,966
Let's go right away.

129
00:05:44,068 --> 00:05:45,336
Short serve.

130
00:05:45,969 --> 00:05:47,938
Look out for a deep serve for me.

131
00:05:47,938 --> 00:05:49,807
(The home-court atmosphere
shaking the pro team)

132
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:52,109
The first one to serve
from Wonder Dogs is Seung Ju.

133
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:59,416
- Clap, everyone.
- Pyo Seung Ju.

134
00:05:59,416 --> 00:06:00,617
One more time.

135
00:06:00,617 --> 00:06:04,488
Even a really old fan of mine is
at the match today.

136
00:06:04,488 --> 00:06:05,656
I'm so grateful.

137
00:06:05,956 --> 00:06:07,624
I had mixed feelings.

138
00:06:08,092 --> 00:06:09,626
- Pyo Seung Ju.
- Pyo Seung Ju.

139
00:06:09,626 --> 00:06:11,204
Clap, everyone.

140
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:12,773
(Zone Four for target serve)

141
00:06:12,942 --> 00:06:15,981
(Targeting serve to Zone Four)

142
00:06:17,935 --> 00:06:19,203
Crush it.

143
00:06:19,603 --> 00:06:21,205
(Energized by the fans' cheering,)

144
00:06:21,784 --> 00:06:22,537
(the perfect target serve!)

145
00:06:22,538 --> 00:06:23,639
A shaky receive.

146
00:06:24,475 --> 00:06:25,876
Spike.

147
00:06:27,244 --> 00:06:29,513
- It's out.
- That is an error.

148
00:06:30,447 --> 00:06:32,883
(Yes!)

149
00:06:34,651 --> 00:06:35,819
Let's hear the cheer.

150
00:06:35,819 --> 00:06:36,820
Okay!

151
00:06:38,001 --> 00:06:40,003
(First set, Pink Spiders 1: Wonder Dogs 2)

152
00:06:40,096 --> 00:06:42,549
The target serve was a great hit.

153
00:06:42,550 --> 00:06:45,762
Seung Ju hit a target serve
aimed at Da Eun.

154
00:06:45,762 --> 00:06:47,464
Surprised by the target serve,

155
00:06:47,464 --> 00:06:49,232
the Pink Spiders made an error.

156
00:06:49,233 --> 00:06:51,420
(Forcing an attack error
when setting the ball)

157
00:06:52,762 --> 00:06:54,697
(Keep going
with the Zone Four targeting serve.)

158
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:59,176
The Wonder Dogs are leading,
one point ahead.

159
00:07:03,647 --> 00:07:06,216
A service point!

160
00:07:06,416 --> 00:07:07,222
Yes.

161
00:07:07,223 --> 00:07:09,915
(Captain Pyo's on-point service)

162
00:07:09,916 --> 00:07:12,819
(This is what we are talking about!)

163
00:07:13,178 --> 00:07:15,714
(Cheer song for ace service,
"Bomba" by Jessy Metafor)

164
00:07:16,381 --> 00:07:19,317
(Exhilarating!)

165
00:07:19,318 --> 00:07:21,453
It's only the beginning,
and we are leading by two points.

166
00:07:21,453 --> 00:07:23,118
It's three to one already!

167
00:07:23,119 --> 00:07:25,170
I cannot believe this!

168
00:07:25,624 --> 00:07:28,660
(Seung Ju serving again)

169
00:07:31,530 --> 00:07:33,697
- Alright.
- Their receive is a bit shaky.

170
00:07:33,923 --> 00:07:34,824
A free ball for us.

171
00:07:35,479 --> 00:07:37,848
Song Hee and Na Yeon are
checking both sides.

172
00:07:38,388 --> 00:07:39,456
Let's go!

173
00:07:39,457 --> 00:07:40,636
(Myoung Hwa is soaring.)

174
00:07:40,636 --> 00:07:41,573
Okay, okay.

175
00:07:42,374 --> 00:07:45,711
- Okay.
- A feint tip from the middle!

176
00:07:45,711 --> 00:07:47,746
(Quick Myoung Hwa did it again.)

177
00:07:49,448 --> 00:07:51,550
(Amazing!)

178
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:53,064
I'm getting goosebumps!

179
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:57,789
The middle and setter attackers...

180
00:07:57,789 --> 00:07:59,791
played great roles
in the last match as well.

181
00:08:00,277 --> 00:08:02,513
(Previous match against Red Sparks)

182
00:08:03,288 --> 00:08:05,790
(With quick transition attacks,)

183
00:08:06,391 --> 00:08:08,994
(she ruled the center
of the Wonder Dogs court.)

184
00:08:09,761 --> 00:08:11,763
(Her name is Quick Myoung Hwa now.)

185
00:08:11,763 --> 00:08:15,433
Myoung Hwa wins the first point
of today's match,

186
00:08:15,434 --> 00:08:18,037
not from blocking, but from attacking.

187
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:21,072
It's four to one, three points ahead.

188
00:08:21,813 --> 00:08:23,348
Seung Ju's service.

189
00:08:25,008 --> 00:08:26,643
Su Been. Da Sol.

190
00:08:27,377 --> 00:08:28,311
Spike!

191
00:08:28,946 --> 00:08:29,780
My ball!

192
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,615
They save it. Hye In.

193
00:08:31,615 --> 00:08:33,183
A second-ball set to the right.

194
00:08:33,183 --> 00:08:34,251
Spike!

195
00:08:35,085 --> 00:08:37,487
Da Sol sets it up long,
and Su Been receives.

196
00:08:37,821 --> 00:08:39,389
Ji Yun on the right.

197
00:08:39,389 --> 00:08:40,857
(Ball is in Ji Yun's hands.)

198
00:08:40,857 --> 00:08:41,825
It's out.

199
00:08:42,659 --> 00:08:44,561
It's out! Okay!

200
00:08:45,529 --> 00:08:47,564
(It's out.)

201
00:08:47,998 --> 00:08:49,366
(Four points in a row?)

202
00:08:49,366 --> 00:08:50,534
Yes.

203
00:08:51,768 --> 00:08:53,002
It was a touch.

204
00:08:53,704 --> 00:08:54,805
That was not a touch?

205
00:08:55,872 --> 00:08:58,274
(It was no touch.)

206
00:08:58,809 --> 00:08:59,710
Video review.

207
00:09:00,344 --> 00:09:02,646
(The Pink Spiders request a video review.)

208
00:09:03,046 --> 00:09:05,615
The Pink Spiders have requested
a video review.

209
00:09:05,615 --> 00:09:08,251
The Pink Spiders request a video review.

210
00:09:14,157 --> 00:09:15,859
The ball passes by Myoung Hwa.

211
00:09:17,227 --> 00:09:18,795
- It's a touch.
- Yes.

212
00:09:18,795 --> 00:09:20,297
(Touch)

213
00:09:21,365 --> 00:09:23,300
(Disappointed)

214
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,769
The call has been overturned
after the video review.

215
00:09:27,223 --> 00:09:29,892
(Looking relaxed)

216
00:09:29,893 --> 00:09:31,628
(First set, Pink Spiders 2: Wonder Dogs 5)

217
00:09:31,808 --> 00:09:34,577
We have high hopes for this one.
Myoung Hwa serving.

218
00:09:37,139 --> 00:09:38,607
Su Been barely saves it.

219
00:09:38,855 --> 00:09:40,381
(Immediate toss to the left)

220
00:09:41,441 --> 00:09:44,206
Da Eun scores
with a strike down to the line.

221
00:09:45,306 --> 00:09:48,009
It looks like
the Pink Spiders will look to go...

222
00:09:48,022 --> 00:09:50,986
more toward the lower side
rather than the higher side.

223
00:09:50,987 --> 00:09:53,322
Da Eun is also pretty sharp
with her line attacks.

224
00:09:53,323 --> 00:09:54,176
Right.

225
00:09:54,905 --> 00:09:57,941
Why was your blocking too loose?
The gap was this wide.

226
00:09:57,941 --> 00:09:59,468
Stay in your position, okay?

227
00:09:59,468 --> 00:10:00,788
The score gap is two.

228
00:10:00,789 --> 00:10:02,157
(First set, Pink Spiders 3
: Wonder Dogs 5)

229
00:10:02,844 --> 00:10:05,447
(The server is Moon Ji Yun.)

230
00:10:06,256 --> 00:10:08,986
It's a strong serve,
and Song Hee received it safely.

231
00:10:10,269 --> 00:10:13,056
Enkhsoyol changed the ball's direction,
but they defended it.

232
00:10:13,612 --> 00:10:14,612
Spike!

233
00:10:15,819 --> 00:10:18,891
A dig from the back line, and it's time
for the Wonder Dogs to counterattack!

234
00:10:18,975 --> 00:10:20,810
It's okay. Just hit it hard.

235
00:10:21,431 --> 00:10:22,832
(A powerful hit)

236
00:10:23,567 --> 00:10:24,567
She kept the ball alive.

237
00:10:26,096 --> 00:10:28,929
By making that quick back-row defense
on the dink, they buy some time.

238
00:10:28,930 --> 00:10:31,442
As it brushes off Na Yeon's fingertips,
the ball goes to Enkhsoyol.

239
00:10:32,956 --> 00:10:34,257
(It's saved again.)

240
00:10:35,045 --> 00:10:36,179
It was a bit far from her.

241
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:37,581
(The ball went to Da Eun.)

242
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:42,417
(A blocking strategy for each player
prepared by the Pink Spiders master)

243
00:10:42,570 --> 00:10:44,795
(When blocking Da Eun,)

244
00:10:45,030 --> 00:10:47,259
(trap the ball between both hands.)

245
00:10:47,989 --> 00:10:50,124
(As the master has said,
she aims the ball at the middle!)

246
00:10:52,048 --> 00:10:53,048
They blocked it.

247
00:10:53,702 --> 00:10:55,037
(Where's next?)

248
00:10:55,672 --> 00:10:56,672
The ball is set.

249
00:10:57,138 --> 00:10:58,502
A soft tip, but they dug it.

250
00:10:59,307 --> 00:11:01,000
It goes to Enkhsoyol.

251
00:11:01,001 --> 00:11:02,539
(The third attempt by Enkhsoyol)

252
00:11:02,906 --> 00:11:04,241
Do it with confidence.

253
00:11:04,441 --> 00:11:05,842
(Jumping confidently)

254
00:11:06,023 --> 00:11:07,755
Powerful spike!

255
00:11:07,756 --> 00:11:09,108
It's touchout.

256
00:11:09,827 --> 00:11:11,595
(We're so proud of you.)

257
00:11:12,255 --> 00:11:13,790
(Enkhsoyol, our baby!)

258
00:11:15,066 --> 00:11:16,286
Enkhsoyol!

259
00:11:18,681 --> 00:11:19,978
(After a long rally,
Enkhsoyol comes out on top.)

260
00:11:19,979 --> 00:11:24,151
The Wonder Dogs are really pushing hard
from the very start.

261
00:11:24,152 --> 00:11:26,311
Their play has been incredibly clean...

262
00:11:26,312 --> 00:11:29,233
because their touches have
been turning into effective blocks.

263
00:11:29,234 --> 00:11:31,929
They are creating
their own chance balls...

264
00:11:31,930 --> 00:11:35,151
and turning their practiced patterns
into fast plays on the court.

265
00:11:35,151 --> 00:11:36,325
That is right.

266
00:11:36,662 --> 00:11:38,362
The score is 7 to 3 with a 4-point lead.

267
00:11:39,276 --> 00:11:41,111
(A serve by Song Hee)

268
00:11:41,688 --> 00:11:44,148
It goes to Eun Ji,
and Da Sol set it backward.

269
00:11:44,874 --> 00:11:47,424
- They keep the ball alive.
- Good.

270
00:11:47,793 --> 00:11:48,803
(Responding with a quick moving attack)

271
00:11:50,886 --> 00:11:51,886
A quick attack to the middle!

272
00:11:53,590 --> 00:11:54,458
Cover it!

273
00:11:55,843 --> 00:11:57,076
They managed to save it.

274
00:11:57,077 --> 00:11:58,328
(The Pink Spiders' chance ball)

275
00:11:58,799 --> 00:11:59,799
Again!

276
00:12:02,056 --> 00:12:03,764
(Strategy to counter Ji Su)

277
00:12:05,468 --> 00:12:08,170
Just twist the block slightly like this.
Understood?

278
00:12:08,171 --> 00:12:09,775
(Understood.)

279
00:12:09,929 --> 00:12:10,897
(Slightly twisted block!)

280
00:12:12,923 --> 00:12:15,279
A great save by...

281
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:17,262
- Enkhsoyol!
- Enkhsoyol!

282
00:12:22,604 --> 00:12:24,206
(I knew it.)

283
00:12:24,706 --> 00:12:26,708
(Proud)

284
00:12:26,709 --> 00:12:30,731
Enkhsoyol is now
an ace of the Wonder Dogs.

285
00:12:32,379 --> 00:12:35,004
The ball goes long. It goes to our court.

286
00:12:36,023 --> 00:12:39,422
- Enkhsoyol lands the spike.
- Enkhsoyol!

287
00:12:40,288 --> 00:12:42,757
(The fans are smiling ear to ear,
thanks to the ace's performance.)

288
00:12:43,458 --> 00:12:45,961
(Meanwhile, someone starts to fret.)

289
00:12:45,962 --> 00:12:47,568
Yun Ju!

290
00:12:50,255 --> 00:12:54,146
In the end,
the Pink Spiders bring in Yun Ju.

291
00:12:54,166 --> 00:12:56,510
They put her
in a bit earlier than expected.

292
00:12:57,427 --> 00:13:01,758
They put the national team players
into the game,

293
00:13:02,294 --> 00:13:03,794
and I really like it.

294
00:13:04,357 --> 00:13:06,493
It's a chance to test our team.

295
00:13:06,808 --> 00:13:10,789
This gives me such a thrill.
I enjoy it so much.

296
00:13:11,538 --> 00:13:15,232
She scored 432 points
in the previous league.

297
00:13:15,576 --> 00:13:16,909
(Excited)

298
00:13:17,350 --> 00:13:19,485
(A targeted attack on Zone Four again)

299
00:13:21,808 --> 00:13:23,576
(A targeted attack on Zone Four)

300
00:13:24,135 --> 00:13:26,371
(Amid tense anticipation,)

301
00:13:27,032 --> 00:13:29,701
(Song Hee serves.)

302
00:13:33,246 --> 00:13:36,416
The serve hits right on the line!

303
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:38,684
(Told you. It's thrilling.)

304
00:13:40,946 --> 00:13:42,148
Song Hee, great job!

305
00:13:42,615 --> 00:13:44,817
(The little giant took down
the national team player.)

306
00:13:45,665 --> 00:13:46,792
Na Yeon.

307
00:13:47,707 --> 00:13:50,100
A run is fine,
but when the ball drops a bit far,

308
00:13:50,101 --> 00:13:52,699
- try going for a middle back attack.
- Okay.

309
00:13:53,113 --> 00:13:57,049
The score is 10 to 3.
The Wonder Dogs are leading by 7 points.

310
00:13:58,724 --> 00:14:00,193
The game continues with Song Hee's serve.

311
00:14:01,975 --> 00:14:03,368
The reception is shaky.

312
00:14:04,370 --> 00:14:07,001
They can't go for the hit,
so it's our freeball.

313
00:14:07,002 --> 00:14:08,530
The Wonder Dogs should stay in the lead.

314
00:14:08,955 --> 00:14:10,855
(A middle toss as planned)

315
00:14:12,308 --> 00:14:14,147
A middle back attack!

316
00:14:14,702 --> 00:14:16,402
(What an endless blessing of scores!)

317
00:14:16,403 --> 00:14:18,172
Now their attacks have become more varied.

318
00:14:18,288 --> 00:14:23,438
The whole team is syncing up perfectly.

319
00:14:23,438 --> 00:14:25,608
Their serve strategy is solid,

320
00:14:25,998 --> 00:14:28,288
and the player receiving the first ball...

321
00:14:28,289 --> 00:14:30,447
during counterattacks is
reacting really well.

322
00:14:30,454 --> 00:14:33,001
That's why even better plays are
coming out more and more.

323
00:14:33,955 --> 00:14:38,076
(Seamless plays by the Wonder Dogs)

324
00:14:44,766 --> 00:14:48,567
(The Pink Spiders' timeout)

325
00:14:52,451 --> 00:14:56,407
They might read Da Sol setting the ball
to Yun Ju...

326
00:14:56,408 --> 00:14:59,434
and come up to the block.
Then just tip it over. Okay?

327
00:15:02,175 --> 00:15:04,711
(The Wonder Dogs quickly form
a double block,)

328
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:07,809
(and they use it to aim
for a blocker-out play.)

329
00:15:08,257 --> 00:15:11,093
- Let's do this.
- Let's go!

330
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:14,884
Spikers, hit it! We've got you covered.

331
00:15:15,737 --> 00:15:17,524
(Two national attackers are at the net.)

332
00:15:17,525 --> 00:15:19,288
You're doing fine. Just set it high.

333
00:15:19,682 --> 00:15:23,525
- Serve hard to the spot I tell you. Okay?
- Yes!

334
00:15:23,526 --> 00:15:25,093
- In 1, 2, 3.
- Let's go!

335
00:15:25,094 --> 00:15:26,688
(Let's continue our momentum!)

336
00:15:26,689 --> 00:15:28,263
Focus more!

337
00:15:28,934 --> 00:15:31,159
The Wonder Dogs are leading
by eight points.

338
00:15:31,167 --> 00:15:31,923
(The serve is still with Song Hee.)

339
00:15:32,368 --> 00:15:34,804
(Yun Ju, you know it, right?)

340
00:15:39,601 --> 00:15:40,669
Left!

341
00:15:42,321 --> 00:15:43,375
(A soft dink by Yun Ju)

342
00:15:44,049 --> 00:15:45,482
A soft dink, but it's blocked.

343
00:15:45,483 --> 00:15:47,337
Hit it now!

344
00:15:48,037 --> 00:15:49,438
(The ball is set to Yun Ju again.)

345
00:15:50,753 --> 00:15:52,455
(Isn't she jumping a bit too early?)

346
00:15:54,152 --> 00:15:55,965
On the spot, she hits it hard!

347
00:15:56,578 --> 00:15:57,904
Nice job!

348
00:15:57,905 --> 00:16:00,083
- Yun Ju has such powerful hits.
- Right.

349
00:16:01,010 --> 00:16:03,512
(Our plan worked!)

350
00:16:04,087 --> 00:16:05,922
Dang it.

351
00:16:06,396 --> 00:16:07,931
It was a bit too early, right?

352
00:16:09,057 --> 00:16:10,692
(A serve by Yun Ju)

353
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:13,540
- She has a really solid serve.
- Right.

354
00:16:13,872 --> 00:16:16,967
Stay in between.

355
00:16:17,205 --> 00:16:18,501
It'll drop sharply.

356
00:16:18,502 --> 00:16:20,323
(Watch out for the ball dropping.)

357
00:16:20,852 --> 00:16:21,852
The score is 11 to 4.

358
00:16:21,853 --> 00:16:23,322
(First set, Pink Spiders 4
: Wonder Dogs 11)

359
00:16:25,515 --> 00:16:27,125
(The sharply dropping serve)

360
00:16:27,125 --> 00:16:28,203
It was a powerful serve.

361
00:16:29,410 --> 00:16:32,083
(The toss is falling far from the net.)

362
00:16:33,642 --> 00:16:35,177
(straight out of bounds.)

363
00:16:35,805 --> 00:16:37,454
- It's my mistake.
- Enkhsoyol, you're rushing too much.

364
00:16:37,455 --> 00:16:38,551
It was too far from the net.

365
00:16:38,552 --> 00:16:40,325
They need to be cautious of this.

366
00:16:40,326 --> 00:16:41,993
Set it up!

367
00:16:42,910 --> 00:16:43,910
It's 11 to 5.

368
00:16:43,911 --> 00:16:45,096
(A serve by Yun Ju, who is on a roll.)

369
00:16:48,433 --> 00:16:50,268
(Another shaky reception)

370
00:16:53,405 --> 00:16:55,307
(The toss has completely collapsed.)

371
00:16:55,601 --> 00:16:56,641
A short dink.

372
00:16:57,294 --> 00:16:58,309
Eun Ji set it.

373
00:16:59,217 --> 00:17:00,485
(The ball goes to Ji Yun on the right.)

374
00:17:00,486 --> 00:17:01,488
Just tip it over.

375
00:17:03,056 --> 00:17:04,782
A hard hit to the right.

376
00:17:04,783 --> 00:17:06,885
(They immediately returned it
with a strong spike.)

377
00:17:07,881 --> 00:17:09,821
- They're back in the game.
- Yes.

378
00:17:10,711 --> 00:17:11,711
Yun Ju set it.

379
00:17:11,712 --> 00:17:13,091
(The game continues.)

380
00:17:13,203 --> 00:17:14,203
It's Eun Ji.

381
00:17:14,204 --> 00:17:17,262
(Will it be another block touch?)

382
00:17:18,496 --> 00:17:19,496
Song Hee keeps the ball alive!

383
00:17:20,865 --> 00:17:26,070
(I'll save the ball, no matter what!)

384
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:33,106
But she failed to keep it alive.

385
00:17:33,804 --> 00:17:36,807
(No way.)

386
00:17:37,382 --> 00:17:39,985
Hey!

387
00:17:41,086 --> 00:17:43,597
I'm sorry. I should've handled it.

388
00:17:44,331 --> 00:17:46,772
Of course, you should have!

389
00:17:47,635 --> 00:17:49,575
(The flow is getting tricky.)

390
00:17:49,897 --> 00:17:51,390
The score gap is only four now.

391
00:17:53,373 --> 00:17:56,134
(With Myoung Hwa, a wall on the court,
leading the way,)

392
00:17:56,904 --> 00:18:02,109
(the Wonder Dogs' greatest strength
has been their blocking.)

393
00:18:02,754 --> 00:18:05,757
(But today,)

394
00:18:07,379 --> 00:18:10,682
(they're helpless
against the tip-over strategy.)

395
00:18:11,249 --> 00:18:14,285
(It's their first match
with their supporters' presence.)

396
00:18:14,692 --> 00:18:17,578
(So, they must prove themselves.)

397
00:18:17,732 --> 00:18:21,023
- Guys, we need to mind the score.
- Okay!

398
00:18:22,093 --> 00:18:25,463
(First set, Pink Spiders 8
: Wonder Dogs 12)

399
00:18:25,864 --> 00:18:27,632
(A serve by Ji Su)

400
00:18:31,202 --> 00:18:32,437
(Tossing to Seung Ju)

401
00:18:32,716 --> 00:18:36,508
- Seung Ju scores easily with a spike.
- Great.

402
00:18:37,763 --> 00:18:40,299
(That is it!)

403
00:18:40,955 --> 00:18:43,140
(The attacking strategy
of the rookie coach)

404
00:18:43,141 --> 00:18:45,654
Hit it long
while keeping the spiker in mind.

405
00:18:45,654 --> 00:18:47,833
But what if you can't go for it?

406
00:18:48,266 --> 00:18:51,906
Hit it to Zone Three.
Make sure to remember this.

407
00:18:51,906 --> 00:18:54,192
- And don't let them block it. Got it?
- Yes.

408
00:18:55,259 --> 00:18:58,062
(As the attacking route down to the line
doesn't seem open,)

409
00:18:58,063 --> 00:19:00,999
(they went right for Zone Three.)

410
00:19:02,452 --> 00:19:04,371
Seung Ju ended the scoring streak
against them.

411
00:19:05,415 --> 00:19:07,984
(First set, Pink Spiders 8
: Wonder Dogs 13)

412
00:19:10,004 --> 00:19:11,408
Yun Ju made a solid reception.

413
00:19:11,922 --> 00:19:13,290
(Attempting a quick attack to the middle)

414
00:19:14,832 --> 00:19:16,600
(Did the block get through?)

415
00:19:17,395 --> 00:19:19,797
(All that's left is the back row defense.)

416
00:19:21,438 --> 00:19:22,806
(They received it!)

417
00:19:23,619 --> 00:19:26,722
(And the ball goes to Seung Ju.)

418
00:19:32,551 --> 00:19:35,198
Seung Ju goes for it.
The block deflects out!

419
00:19:35,833 --> 00:19:36,391
(Cheering)

420
00:19:38,652 --> 00:19:41,652
(We knew Captain Pyo could do it!)

421
00:19:41,653 --> 00:19:42,719
Pyo Seung Ju!

422
00:19:43,919 --> 00:19:46,377
(Captain Pyo's scoring streak
changes the atmosphere.)

423
00:19:46,866 --> 00:19:49,366
Once Pyo Seung Ju joined,

424
00:19:49,366 --> 00:19:52,199
the Wonder Dogs' balance
of attack and defense got better.

425
00:19:52,199 --> 00:19:53,199
Of course.

426
00:19:54,085 --> 00:19:56,818
(Their tricky play brings applause.)

427
00:19:57,905 --> 00:20:00,205
(The Wonder Dogs are on a momentum.)

428
00:20:02,555 --> 00:20:04,055
Kim Da Sol's back toss.

429
00:20:06,101 --> 00:20:08,068
(Is it a block touch out once more?)

430
00:20:09,301 --> 00:20:10,768
She saved this!

431
00:20:10,768 --> 00:20:11,868
(Koo Hye In's coverage)

432
00:20:12,568 --> 00:20:14,001
(We won't miss it...)

433
00:20:14,001 --> 00:20:15,534
(this time!)

434
00:20:15,534 --> 00:20:16,568
Come on!

435
00:20:16,568 --> 00:20:17,634
(Hurry!)

436
00:20:21,234 --> 00:20:22,234
Hey!

437
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:30,126
Their play today isn't that bad,

438
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:33,188
but they tend to miss
some of the attacks they spot.

439
00:20:33,188 --> 00:20:34,547
(They already lost two points
from their mistakes.)

440
00:20:35,521 --> 00:20:36,521
My mistake.

441
00:20:39,667 --> 00:20:41,033
(Checking the replay screen)

442
00:20:41,033 --> 00:20:44,633
Hey, where are you looking?
You should do it!

443
00:20:46,484 --> 00:20:47,551
My mistake!

444
00:20:48,951 --> 00:20:50,518
It's okay. Let's do it again.

445
00:20:53,051 --> 00:20:54,518
Is that girl crazy?

446
00:20:55,724 --> 00:20:57,291
(I think she's angry.)

447
00:20:57,291 --> 00:20:58,291
(Coach Kim.)

448
00:20:58,591 --> 00:21:00,624
(Enkhsoyol is scared of her.)

449
00:21:00,937 --> 00:21:02,204
They're now three points apart.

450
00:21:02,205 --> 00:21:04,434
(First set, Pink Spiders 12:
Wonder Dogs 15)

451
00:21:05,208 --> 00:21:06,208
(Choi Eun Ji serves.)
Choi Eun Ji.

452
00:21:07,308 --> 00:21:09,174
Go!

453
00:21:10,208 --> 00:21:11,208
Han Song Hee.

454
00:21:12,608 --> 00:21:13,808
They defended it.

455
00:21:15,341 --> 00:21:16,541
The ball goes to Jeong Yun Ju again.

456
00:21:16,541 --> 00:21:17,574
(Yun Ju's chance to counterattack)

457
00:21:18,337 --> 00:21:19,841
Spike!

458
00:21:19,841 --> 00:21:21,674
A score with a blockout.

459
00:21:21,674 --> 00:21:23,774
This means they're now two points apart.

460
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:25,941
I block too fast.

461
00:21:27,147 --> 00:21:28,647
Myoung Hwa!

462
00:21:29,774 --> 00:21:32,674
Watch your timing.
Jump a bit late to block.

463
00:21:32,674 --> 00:21:34,508
(You must jump later!)

464
00:21:37,173 --> 00:21:38,640
(Jeong Yun Ju again)

465
00:21:39,292 --> 00:21:41,192
(She tries to jump in time.)

466
00:21:44,346 --> 00:21:46,079
Yun Ju scores with a push shot.

467
00:21:46,353 --> 00:21:47,586
(First set, Pink Spiders 14:
Wonder Dogs 16)

468
00:21:47,972 --> 00:21:49,139
Yun Ju runs in.

469
00:21:49,140 --> 00:21:50,140
Spike!

470
00:21:51,107 --> 00:21:52,340
(Also spiking with ease)

471
00:21:52,340 --> 00:21:53,407
She made it.

472
00:21:53,839 --> 00:21:55,039
It's okay.

473
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,307
Jeong Yun Ju also won...

474
00:21:57,340 --> 00:21:59,039
an overall champion last season.

475
00:21:59,039 --> 00:22:00,672
So she improved a lot.

476
00:22:01,072 --> 00:22:02,172
She set the ball up.

477
00:22:02,172 --> 00:22:03,272
(A chance to hit at last)

478
00:22:03,272 --> 00:22:04,672
Enkhsoyol attacks after a pause!

479
00:22:04,672 --> 00:22:05,872
(Blocking immediately)

480
00:22:06,304 --> 00:22:07,370
Going to Yun Ju again!

481
00:22:07,870 --> 00:22:09,670
(When Yun Ju hits,)

482
00:22:09,670 --> 00:22:10,670
Spike!

483
00:22:10,683 --> 00:22:13,246
Jeong Yun Ju.

484
00:22:13,247 --> 00:22:14,345
(they score no matter what.)

485
00:22:14,704 --> 00:22:17,604
They're now just a single point apart.

486
00:22:18,037 --> 00:22:20,037
In a way, Yun Ju learned...

487
00:22:20,037 --> 00:22:22,604
many techniques from Coach Kim as well.

488
00:22:22,604 --> 00:22:25,537
- She gained a lot.
- Yes.

489
00:22:31,443 --> 00:22:35,876
(The Wonder Dogs' timeout)

490
00:22:39,302 --> 00:22:40,969
Enkhsoyol, when you're hitting,

491
00:22:41,156 --> 00:22:42,623
where does the blocker at Zone Six go?

492
00:22:42,623 --> 00:22:44,756
- She goes back to the left.
- She comes back here.

493
00:22:45,923 --> 00:22:49,993
(When Enkhsoyol aims for the gap
between the blockers,)

494
00:22:50,942 --> 00:22:55,242
(she stealthily comes in advance to dig.)

495
00:22:55,623 --> 00:22:57,556
Why do you keep attacking here?
They'll defend.

496
00:22:57,556 --> 00:22:58,790
- Hit here.
- Yes, Coach.

497
00:22:58,790 --> 00:23:00,490
There's a lot of space.
Attack here otherwise.

498
00:23:00,490 --> 00:23:02,823
- Yes, Coach.
- Hit here. You know she comes back.

499
00:23:02,823 --> 00:23:04,023
- Yes.
- Got it?

500
00:23:04,323 --> 00:23:05,723
How does Su Yeon serve?

501
00:23:05,723 --> 00:23:07,456
- It's a bit short.
- She has a short serve.

502
00:23:07,456 --> 00:23:09,123
So take a step in to catch.

503
00:23:09,123 --> 00:23:10,123
- Yes.
- Yes.

504
00:23:10,123 --> 00:23:11,423
- Let's go!
- Just one more point.

505
00:23:11,423 --> 00:23:12,800
In 1, 2, 3!

506
00:23:13,361 --> 00:23:15,594
(We won't let them turn the tables!)

507
00:23:16,018 --> 00:23:18,951
Let's all applaud the players!

508
00:23:22,851 --> 00:23:26,285
It's 17 to 16, and the Wonder Dogs are
being chased with just a point behind.

509
00:23:26,451 --> 00:23:28,485
Although their opponent is after them,

510
00:23:28,485 --> 00:23:29,951
I hope the players could think
that they're...

511
00:23:29,951 --> 00:23:32,608
- a point ahead instead of rushing.
- That's right.

512
00:23:32,609 --> 00:23:33,479
(We're still at an advantage!)

513
00:23:34,031 --> 00:23:36,074
(Park Su Yeon serves.)

514
00:23:36,407 --> 00:23:39,007
(Remember the short serve.)

515
00:23:43,914 --> 00:23:45,814
Park Su Yeon of the Pink Spiders serves.

516
00:23:46,081 --> 00:23:47,214
- Go, Na Yeon!
- Koo Hye In.

517
00:23:47,214 --> 00:23:48,781
(Nice reception)

518
00:23:48,848 --> 00:23:49,848
Hit it!

519
00:23:50,367 --> 00:23:51,933
(The blocker moves outside again.)

520
00:23:52,298 --> 00:23:54,032
(She aims for Zone Six as planned!)

521
00:23:55,465 --> 00:23:57,965
Enkhsoyol spikes!

522
00:23:58,265 --> 00:24:00,632
(Did the strategy work?)

523
00:24:03,365 --> 00:24:04,979
(The Wonder Dogs' net touch)

524
00:24:04,979 --> 00:24:07,012
It's a net touch.

525
00:24:10,598 --> 00:24:12,732
It was a little close,

526
00:24:12,732 --> 00:24:14,265
but her hands touched the net.

527
00:24:16,465 --> 00:24:18,365
Nice!

528
00:24:18,365 --> 00:24:19,565
Let's go!

529
00:24:20,864 --> 00:24:21,864
(Oh, my.)

530
00:24:22,398 --> 00:24:23,832
My mistake.

531
00:24:23,832 --> 00:24:27,998
The Wonder Dogs made an error
for the score to be tied.

532
00:24:28,187 --> 00:24:30,287
Na Yeon, toss it overhand!

533
00:24:30,654 --> 00:24:31,687
Yes, Coach.

534
00:24:32,504 --> 00:24:33,955
(When the team was attacking,)

535
00:24:34,212 --> 00:24:36,989
(Na Yeon did an underhand toss.)

536
00:24:37,415 --> 00:24:39,215
(When she had to toss deeply,)

537
00:24:39,909 --> 00:24:43,215
(Na Yeon got shaky again.)

538
00:24:43,215 --> 00:24:44,215
Sorry.

539
00:24:47,409 --> 00:24:50,075
Enkhsoyol.

540
00:24:50,075 --> 00:24:53,375
(That's it. Keep targeting Zone Six.)

541
00:24:53,375 --> 00:24:54,442
- In between again.
- Yes.

542
00:24:54,442 --> 00:24:55,542
(Roger that.)

543
00:24:56,075 --> 00:24:58,242
(Park Su Yeon serves again.)

544
00:24:58,242 --> 00:25:00,442
It's 17 to 17, which is a tie.

545
00:25:01,805 --> 00:25:03,871
- Go! Hit it!
- It hits the net and goes over.

546
00:25:03,871 --> 00:25:05,338
Hey, hit the ball!

547
00:25:05,626 --> 00:25:09,233
(But the ball falls from the net again?)

548
00:25:10,793 --> 00:25:11,793
(Halting)

549
00:25:12,126 --> 00:25:13,526
Enkhsoyol!

550
00:25:13,526 --> 00:25:15,059
(A bull's eye to Zone Six!)

551
00:25:20,493 --> 00:25:22,659
(The toss was unstable.)

552
00:25:22,659 --> 00:25:24,726
(But she catches the ball in the air.)

553
00:25:25,726 --> 00:25:28,859
(She even followed the plan flawlessly.)

554
00:25:29,226 --> 00:25:31,463
(The opposing player heads
to defend the gap between blockers.)

555
00:25:31,633 --> 00:25:34,800
(But she does a reverse action.)

556
00:25:35,973 --> 00:25:37,039
Nice.

557
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:38,702
(Meanwhile,
Na Yeon is not in good condition.)

558
00:25:39,517 --> 00:25:40,551
Don't you think Koo Sol is better?

559
00:25:40,751 --> 00:25:41,951
- At sending a ball high?
- Yes.

560
00:25:42,944 --> 00:25:44,083
Sol.

561
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:44,989
(Koo Sol is in.)

562
00:25:45,936 --> 00:25:48,470
(A decision to strengthen attacks
at the end of the set)

563
00:25:48,760 --> 00:25:51,793
Near the end of the set,
Koo Sol goes in...

564
00:25:51,793 --> 00:25:53,126
to wrap up the game.

565
00:25:53,353 --> 00:25:54,353
Let's go.

566
00:25:54,354 --> 00:25:55,923
(While the Wonder Dogs
substitute players,)

567
00:25:56,759 --> 00:25:59,690
(they send signs.)

568
00:26:00,131 --> 00:26:01,931
(Hitters understand.)

569
00:26:02,368 --> 00:26:04,668
There are two hitters!

570
00:26:04,668 --> 00:26:05,835
- Check if they miss the quick.
- Okay.

571
00:26:05,835 --> 00:26:07,101
Double hitters!

572
00:26:10,001 --> 00:26:11,201
Han Song Hee is the server.

573
00:26:11,201 --> 00:26:13,178
(Han Song Hee serves.)

574
00:26:15,219 --> 00:26:16,116
Cover her!

575
00:26:16,117 --> 00:26:17,178
(Jeong Yun Ju again?)

576
00:26:17,598 --> 00:26:19,665
(Opposite side this time)

577
00:26:19,665 --> 00:26:20,698
She did it.

578
00:26:27,298 --> 00:26:30,165
(Attacking blocks once more)

579
00:26:30,165 --> 00:26:31,231
Hey!

580
00:26:33,798 --> 00:26:35,031
(The game continues.)

581
00:26:35,031 --> 00:26:37,065
A powerful serve,
and they received it well.

582
00:26:37,431 --> 00:26:39,198
Enkhsoyol again!

583
00:26:40,144 --> 00:26:41,144
- Yes!
- She scores!

584
00:26:41,145 --> 00:26:42,811
That was a nice hitting point.

585
00:26:43,465 --> 00:26:44,892
That's it!

586
00:26:44,892 --> 00:26:46,131
(When they score by hitting Zone Six,)

587
00:26:46,131 --> 00:26:47,765
Nice toss!

588
00:26:51,617 --> 00:26:52,717
Toss and receive.

589
00:26:53,317 --> 00:26:54,317
Moving attack.

590
00:26:55,252 --> 00:26:56,801
(the others attack blocks again.)

591
00:26:56,801 --> 00:26:58,886
- It's a block out.
- Great job!

592
00:26:59,030 --> 00:27:03,119
(The opponent continues
to keep the score tied.)

593
00:27:03,888 --> 00:27:06,021
- Go!
- The ball is up, and Choi Eun Ji!

594
00:27:06,154 --> 00:27:07,888
(To be broken through...)

595
00:27:07,888 --> 00:27:09,554
They did it.

596
00:27:09,567 --> 00:27:12,300
(First set, Pink Spiders 20
: Wonder Dogs 21)

597
00:27:13,188 --> 00:27:15,121
Pyo Seung Ju and Koo Sol.

598
00:27:15,488 --> 00:27:16,821
Spike!

599
00:27:16,821 --> 00:27:18,588
(or to break through.)

600
00:27:21,754 --> 00:27:24,754
(First set, Pink Spiders 21
: Wonder Dogs 22)

601
00:27:24,988 --> 00:27:27,354
(They're still leading by a point.)

602
00:27:27,714 --> 00:27:29,414
- It's a high ball!
- The reception is short.

603
00:27:29,415 --> 00:27:30,782
(Once again...)

604
00:27:31,008 --> 00:27:32,008
Jeong Yun Ju!

605
00:27:33,780 --> 00:27:34,947
Okay!

606
00:27:34,948 --> 00:27:36,714
(Did the spike fail this time?)

607
00:27:38,060 --> 00:27:39,693
(Out...)

608
00:27:39,693 --> 00:27:42,660
(versus touch out)

609
00:27:43,493 --> 00:27:44,493
It's out!

610
00:27:50,493 --> 00:27:51,493
They touched!

611
00:27:52,339 --> 00:27:53,877
(Let's press it.)

612
00:27:54,921 --> 00:27:56,621
He's asking for a video review.

613
00:27:56,621 --> 00:27:57,921
(Their second request
for a video review in the first set)

614
00:28:06,491 --> 00:28:08,391
- The ball hit it.
- It clearly hit it.

615
00:28:08,391 --> 00:28:10,758
They saw it right before their eyes.

616
00:28:11,825 --> 00:28:13,225
It's ruled as a touchout.

617
00:28:13,225 --> 00:28:14,225
- Okay.
- Well.

618
00:28:14,425 --> 00:28:17,091
It's a touchout,
and the Pink Spiders score.

619
00:28:18,321 --> 00:28:20,621
(A hawk's eye targeting video reviews)

620
00:28:22,379 --> 00:28:23,812
You caught it like this.

621
00:28:23,812 --> 00:28:25,879
Look how you handled the ball.

622
00:28:25,879 --> 00:28:26,912
Where is it?

623
00:28:26,912 --> 00:28:28,612
- It went way past, right?
- Yes.

624
00:28:28,613 --> 00:28:30,665
(Giving feedback on blocking
rather than an immediate error)

625
00:28:31,046 --> 00:28:33,179
Understood? You miss it
because it goes to the middle.

626
00:28:33,179 --> 00:28:35,346
- Got it? You were also too fast.
- Yes, Coach.

627
00:28:35,346 --> 00:28:36,973
(Planning the next move right away)

628
00:28:36,974 --> 00:28:37,907
Chae Rim.

629
00:28:38,769 --> 00:28:39,741
- Chae Rim.
- Chae Rim!

630
00:28:40,228 --> 00:28:44,599
(She waits to get in
as a serving specialist.)

631
00:28:44,853 --> 00:28:46,267
It's 22 to 22, a tie.

632
00:28:48,469 --> 00:28:51,105
(The set is almost coming to an end.)

633
00:28:52,992 --> 00:28:54,181
She manages to set it.

634
00:28:54,181 --> 00:28:55,312
(Setting up the ball carefully)

635
00:28:55,526 --> 00:28:56,965
(Enkhsoyol's spike)

636
00:28:57,875 --> 00:28:59,214
It rises high!

637
00:29:00,087 --> 00:29:01,449
Okay.

638
00:29:01,449 --> 00:29:03,685
It's out!

639
00:29:04,118 --> 00:29:05,493
- It's in!
- In!

640
00:29:05,494 --> 00:29:06,494
It's out.

641
00:29:06,495 --> 00:29:07,989
(She calmly claims it was out.)

642
00:29:08,289 --> 00:29:11,726
(The referee calls it out.)

643
00:29:14,721 --> 00:29:16,016
Is he requesting another review?

644
00:29:16,433 --> 00:29:18,328
He's asking for another video review.

645
00:29:18,329 --> 00:29:19,984
He claims it's in.

646
00:29:21,116 --> 00:29:25,508
This review result
can turn the flow around.

647
00:29:26,136 --> 00:29:27,670
Please. This could be huge.

648
00:29:28,338 --> 00:29:30,073
(Nervous)

649
00:29:30,588 --> 00:29:33,257
(While everyone stays silent,
waiting for the result...)

650
00:29:33,532 --> 00:29:35,667
Chae Rim! Come here.

651
00:29:36,267 --> 00:29:37,668
(But...)

652
00:29:38,797 --> 00:29:40,838
- Chae Rim! Come here.
- It's in.

653
00:29:42,882 --> 00:29:44,725
Who are you to judge here? It's out.

654
00:29:45,363 --> 00:29:47,176
Who are you to judge here? It's out.

655
00:29:52,857 --> 00:29:57,695
(The ball seems to touch from one side,
not the other.)

656
00:29:59,652 --> 00:30:05,291
(The referee's call is...)

657
00:30:07,812 --> 00:30:11,330
The call has changed...

658
00:30:11,391 --> 00:30:12,894
based on the video review.

659
00:30:13,290 --> 00:30:16,068
Now, Pink Spiders are ahead by a point.

660
00:30:17,803 --> 00:30:22,641
(The momentum shifts instantly.)

661
00:30:25,844 --> 00:30:28,680
(Wonder Dogs' timeout)

662
00:30:28,722 --> 00:30:29,782
Come here.

663
00:30:32,937 --> 00:30:33,937
Everyone, gather.

664
00:30:35,093 --> 00:30:36,511
- Everyone!
- Coach's calling everyone!

665
00:30:36,512 --> 00:30:37,626
(Everyone makes a U-turn.)

666
00:30:38,940 --> 00:30:40,460
- Everyone!
- Coach's calling everyone!

667
00:30:47,846 --> 00:30:48,945
- Are you crazy?
- No.

668
00:30:49,390 --> 00:30:50,390
- Are you crazy?
- No.

669
00:30:51,727 --> 00:30:53,341
When the referee didn't call it yet,

670
00:30:53,342 --> 00:30:55,200
you judged it was in
and decided just to stay?

671
00:30:56,364 --> 00:30:57,364
Are you out of your mind?

672
00:30:58,134 --> 00:30:59,749
- Do you think this is a joke?
- No.

673
00:31:01,477 --> 00:31:02,897
What are you doing outside the court?

674
00:31:04,156 --> 00:31:05,343
You think it's a joke?

675
00:31:08,133 --> 00:31:09,825
I can't believe
you're messing with me now.

676
00:31:12,953 --> 00:31:14,268
It was total nonsense.

677
00:31:14,498 --> 00:31:17,622
The score was shifting every minute.

678
00:31:17,970 --> 00:31:20,828
I was so upset to see her behavior then.

679
00:31:21,800 --> 00:31:25,003
(Our goal is
to be a professional team player.)

680
00:31:25,504 --> 00:31:30,743
(In front of our fans
who laugh and cry for us,)

681
00:31:31,363 --> 00:31:35,114
(not a single point...)

682
00:31:36,548 --> 00:31:40,452
(is meaningless.)

683
00:31:41,409 --> 00:31:45,506
This can't happen again.
I tried my best to focus immediately.

684
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:51,760
Focus now.

685
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:55,018
- In 3, 2, 1!
- Go!

686
00:31:55,266 --> 00:31:56,236
Do it right!

687
00:31:56,237 --> 00:32:00,073
Song Hee, you too. If you weren't sure,
you should've received it.

688
00:32:01,577 --> 00:32:02,970
Look at the score now.

689
00:32:02,971 --> 00:32:03,973
We need to stay focused.

690
00:32:05,027 --> 00:32:06,617
When Enkhsoyol hits,

691
00:32:06,946 --> 00:32:09,348
- it's Zone Six.
- Yes.

692
00:32:09,515 --> 00:32:13,003
(Don't move if you're in Zone Six.)

693
00:32:13,470 --> 00:32:14,679
She hasn't hit the straight.

694
00:32:14,680 --> 00:32:17,333
(Every move and every point)

695
00:32:17,756 --> 00:32:20,525
(The pro league champion
never stops chasing.)

696
00:32:20,859 --> 00:32:23,161
(Even a single mistake...)

697
00:32:23,395 --> 00:32:25,831
(might lead the team to defeat.)

698
00:32:26,532 --> 00:32:30,102
(Hye Rim's serve)

699
00:32:35,140 --> 00:32:37,342
She receives it easily.

700
00:32:37,843 --> 00:32:40,713
(The ball is set to Enkhsoyol!)

701
00:32:41,213 --> 00:32:42,815
(Zone Six is ready to receive!)

702
00:32:46,276 --> 00:32:47,465
Enkhsoyol made it!

703
00:32:47,466 --> 00:32:50,255
(It's block out!)

704
00:32:50,761 --> 00:32:51,853
(We're catching them again.)

705
00:32:51,854 --> 00:32:53,545
It was a nice attack.

706
00:32:53,733 --> 00:32:55,218
Did it hit Ji Su's left arm?

707
00:32:55,599 --> 00:32:57,529
It hit Ji Su's left arm, right?

708
00:32:59,077 --> 00:33:01,413
(It means it was heading
to Zone Six anyway.)

709
00:33:01,772 --> 00:33:04,341
(We don't need to change the plan.)

710
00:33:04,522 --> 00:33:06,391
(Meanwhile, the rookie coach...)

711
00:33:06,872 --> 00:33:10,442
(puts Chae Rim on the court as planned.)

712
00:33:10,642 --> 00:33:12,544
Chae Rim, make a nice serve, okay?

713
00:33:14,134 --> 00:33:16,447
Chae Rim gets in to serve.

714
00:33:17,449 --> 00:33:19,318
(Zone Three for target serve)

715
00:33:22,287 --> 00:33:25,590
(Roger that.)

716
00:33:27,650 --> 00:33:28,887
It's tense at a tie.

717
00:33:30,388 --> 00:33:32,618
- Defense!
- The reception was swayed.

718
00:33:32,865 --> 00:33:35,067
(Is she going for a tap?)

719
00:33:35,756 --> 00:33:36,829
Strong spike on the left!

720
00:33:36,830 --> 00:33:38,532
(Enkhsoyol's block)

721
00:33:38,868 --> 00:33:39,868
It's blocked.

722
00:33:40,533 --> 00:33:42,635
- It's a chance.
- Wonder Dogs' chance.

723
00:33:43,968 --> 00:33:46,873
Enkhsoyol!

724
00:33:48,305 --> 00:33:49,425
It's another chance!

725
00:33:49,885 --> 00:33:51,784
(This time...)

726
00:33:51,806 --> 00:33:53,741
(Will it be set to Song Hee or Enkhsoyol?)

727
00:33:57,223 --> 00:33:59,652
She spikes it to the right side!

728
00:34:00,286 --> 00:34:03,030
Song Hee makes up for her earlier mistake!

729
00:34:03,056 --> 00:34:06,430
Song Hee makes up for her earlier mistake!

730
00:34:06,638 --> 00:34:10,108
(The tables have turned again!)

731
00:34:10,530 --> 00:34:15,301
(First Set, Pink Spiders 23
: Wonder Dogs 24)

732
00:34:16,162 --> 00:34:19,950
(Wonder Dogs' set point)

733
00:34:21,941 --> 00:34:23,543
(Buzzing)

734
00:34:24,208 --> 00:34:26,612
Enkhsoyol touched the net while attacking.

735
00:34:27,670 --> 00:34:29,749
Another video review is requested.

736
00:34:31,095 --> 00:34:32,526
Again? What now?

737
00:34:33,736 --> 00:34:36,189
Every time Coach Dae Kyung
requested a review,

738
00:34:36,190 --> 00:34:38,833
his claim has turned out
to be true so far.

739
00:34:40,002 --> 00:34:44,306
(Please, not again.)

740
00:34:49,638 --> 00:34:55,410
(The net doesn't even flinch.)

741
00:34:59,915 --> 00:35:04,586
(It wasn't a net touch violation.)

742
00:35:05,013 --> 00:35:07,215
(After making sure one more time...)

743
00:35:07,636 --> 00:35:09,705
(He admitted it readily.)

744
00:35:10,279 --> 00:35:11,723
(For now, for sure,)

745
00:35:11,723 --> 00:35:14,664
(it's the real set point!)

746
00:35:14,997 --> 00:35:16,198
We can do this, right?

747
00:35:18,192 --> 00:35:19,760
(We can defeat...)

748
00:35:19,935 --> 00:35:23,338
(the pro league champion!)

749
00:35:23,672 --> 00:35:25,199
(With fans cheering loudly...)

750
00:35:25,199 --> 00:35:26,822
Wonder Dogs' set point!

751
00:35:27,543 --> 00:35:28,377
(Here we go!)

752
00:35:29,612 --> 00:35:30,612
Da Sol.

753
00:35:31,091 --> 00:35:32,091
Yun Ju!

754
00:35:33,983 --> 00:35:35,952
(Seung Ju's nice dig)

755
00:35:36,485 --> 00:35:38,087
(Let's do this!)

756
00:35:38,210 --> 00:35:39,255
The defense was successful.

757
00:35:39,547 --> 00:35:40,547
Get it up!

758
00:35:41,257 --> 00:35:43,192
Let's go, Sol!

759
00:35:43,539 --> 00:35:45,341
(And the end of the other side...)

760
00:35:45,628 --> 00:35:46,696
(Enkhsoyol is waiting!)

761
00:35:48,679 --> 00:35:52,134
- Enkhsoyol!
- Spike! It's out!

762
00:35:52,835 --> 00:35:54,937
(Shouting)

763
00:35:58,774 --> 00:36:01,844
(Against the league champion,)

764
00:36:02,144 --> 00:36:05,375
(Wonder Dogs win the first set!)

765
00:36:05,376 --> 00:36:10,317
Wonder Dogs win the first set!

766
00:36:10,719 --> 00:36:12,120
(Thank you!)

767
00:36:13,656 --> 00:36:15,925
(Oh, right. I need to get them towels!)

768
00:36:16,258 --> 00:36:19,895
(Timeout before the second set)

769
00:36:23,713 --> 00:36:25,375
Is the game over?

770
00:36:25,376 --> 00:36:27,375
- No.
- We just won a set.

771
00:36:27,387 --> 00:36:29,917
How can we win? We need the next two sets.

772
00:36:29,934 --> 00:36:31,922
You, Chae Rim. Are you a referee?

773
00:36:32,197 --> 00:36:33,545
Do you want to change uniforms
with the referee?

774
00:36:33,649 --> 00:36:36,791
You're acting
like you all lost your minds.

775
00:36:36,808 --> 00:36:39,260
- Act like you're supposed to.
- Yes, ma'am.

776
00:36:40,061 --> 00:36:42,263
(The newbie coach is angry
at her players' loose mindset.)

777
00:36:42,659 --> 00:36:45,800
Guys, we're still
in the middle of a game, right?

778
00:36:45,849 --> 00:36:48,369
We barely won the first set.

779
00:36:48,566 --> 00:36:51,372
Let's concentrate a little more.
This is our last game.

780
00:36:53,734 --> 00:36:56,777
On the side, Number 14, Yun Ju...

781
00:36:57,104 --> 00:36:59,917
How do Yun Ju and Eun Ji hit the ball?
They push it.

782
00:36:59,925 --> 00:37:01,248
So time before the block.

783
00:37:01,976 --> 00:37:04,178
(The opponents' speciality, push-hitting)

784
00:37:05,557 --> 00:37:07,959
(It made The Wonder Dogs helplessly
lose points by blockout.)

785
00:37:08,205 --> 00:37:10,943
- Time before you block it out. Got it?
- Got it.

786
00:37:10,944 --> 00:37:13,213
Watch out if it's long or not.
It's spray-hitting.

787
00:37:13,214 --> 00:37:15,661
Let's go. Let's get them.

788
00:37:15,812 --> 00:37:17,826
The first set was 25 to 23.

789
00:37:18,487 --> 00:37:20,902
The attack success rate is 47 percent
for Wonder Dogs...

790
00:37:20,928 --> 00:37:22,672
and 50 percent for Pink Spiders.

791
00:37:23,094 --> 00:37:27,077
The biggest challenge is
figuring out how to stop Yun Ju...

792
00:37:27,346 --> 00:37:29,346
with a 70 percent success rate.

793
00:37:29,580 --> 00:37:32,848
In the second set,
she's in the starting lineup.

794
00:37:33,842 --> 00:37:35,911
(Will they be able to catch up?)

795
00:37:36,231 --> 00:37:38,500
(Will they be able
to secure their win here?)

796
00:37:38,917 --> 00:37:42,754
(Only one winner can stand on the court.)

797
00:37:43,460 --> 00:37:45,731
(Move ahead to victory!)

798
00:37:45,958 --> 00:37:46,958
The second set begins.

799
00:37:48,006 --> 00:37:49,808
(Na Yeon's serve)

800
00:37:53,044 --> 00:37:54,979
(Let's go!)

801
00:38:00,435 --> 00:38:02,780
Spike to the right. She receives it.

802
00:38:04,137 --> 00:38:05,137
Song Hee.

803
00:38:05,613 --> 00:38:06,991
Seung Ju, go!

804
00:38:07,146 --> 00:38:09,181
(The ball is set to Seung Ju.)

805
00:38:09,674 --> 00:38:11,342
Where do you think the defender
in Zone Six will go?

806
00:38:11,503 --> 00:38:13,105
She turns here.

807
00:38:13,293 --> 00:38:15,128
There's no one. Just hit it to Zone Six.

808
00:38:16,396 --> 00:38:18,031
(Seung Ju jumps up.)

809
00:38:18,465 --> 00:38:19,967
(And she makes a turn.)

810
00:38:22,909 --> 00:38:25,677
Seung Ju's tip! It's a success!

811
00:38:26,306 --> 00:38:28,475
(Zone Six was spot on!)

812
00:38:30,336 --> 00:38:33,513
Pyo Seung Ju!

813
00:38:33,952 --> 00:38:35,990
Wonder Dogs start ahead.

814
00:38:38,236 --> 00:38:39,730
(Hitting the net and deflecting)

815
00:38:41,372 --> 00:38:42,873
(Ji Yun flies up.)

816
00:38:45,577 --> 00:38:47,746
(Spike)

817
00:38:49,387 --> 00:38:50,721
Nice attack.

818
00:38:50,721 --> 00:38:51,655
(Point off the block)
Is it out?

819
00:38:52,423 --> 00:38:53,758
(Another block-out
continuing into set two.)

820
00:38:53,758 --> 00:38:55,826
She hits when the ball drops.
She takes her time.

821
00:38:55,826 --> 00:38:57,361
- She hits it when the ball drops.
- Okay.

822
00:38:57,361 --> 00:38:59,897
It's 1 to 1 now.
The Pink Spiders are catching up.

823
00:39:00,198 --> 00:39:02,254
(Ji Yun serving)

824
00:39:03,122 --> 00:39:04,390
Perfect reception.

825
00:39:05,691 --> 00:39:07,259
(And spike)

826
00:39:09,228 --> 00:39:10,930
(Yun Ju hitting)

827
00:39:11,463 --> 00:39:12,431
Defense is up!

828
00:39:12,431 --> 00:39:14,566
(Hye In's diving dig)

829
00:39:15,234 --> 00:39:17,103
(The ball goes over
to the opponent's court.)

830
00:39:17,903 --> 00:39:18,837
Back to Yun Ju.

831
00:39:18,837 --> 00:39:20,072
(The ball is in Yun Ju's hands.)

832
00:39:22,474 --> 00:39:23,275
Spike!

833
00:39:24,410 --> 00:39:26,412
That was a big bounce.
They've got to save it.

834
00:39:26,412 --> 00:39:27,747
(The ball hit her hand and flew off.)

835
00:39:30,816 --> 00:39:33,919
(Will this be another blocker touch-out?)

836
00:39:37,956 --> 00:39:39,850
- Enkhsoyol saves it!
- She saved it!

837
00:39:40,992 --> 00:39:42,694
Enkhsoyol's hustle play!

838
00:39:42,981 --> 00:39:44,816
(Screaming in excitement)

839
00:39:45,296 --> 00:39:47,158
- Nice defense!
- Nice!

840
00:39:47,986 --> 00:39:49,353
(The ball is saved and set.)

841
00:39:49,827 --> 00:39:50,668
Song Hee!
(Song Hee's spike)

842
00:39:51,951 --> 00:39:52,818
Alright.

843
00:39:54,019 --> 00:39:55,253
They can't attack at the moment.

844
00:39:55,254 --> 00:39:56,655
(An intense rally continues)

845
00:39:58,290 --> 00:40:00,626
Middle attack,
we save it again, and continue.

846
00:40:00,679 --> 00:40:03,062
(If the middle is blocked,
then we go left.)

847
00:40:03,464 --> 00:40:05,616
(Small giant coming again)

848
00:40:06,165 --> 00:40:07,433
Song Hee!

849
00:40:07,554 --> 00:40:09,689
(Point off the block)

850
00:40:09,689 --> 00:40:10,623
Yes!

851
00:40:10,824 --> 00:40:12,259
(This is insane!)

852
00:40:13,427 --> 00:40:16,663
Enkhsoyol's unbelievable diving catch!

853
00:40:17,631 --> 00:40:19,833
Great job. That's how we defend.

854
00:40:20,538 --> 00:40:22,807
By the end, we successfully attacked...

855
00:40:22,807 --> 00:40:24,842
and won the point,

856
00:40:24,976 --> 00:40:26,844
but this kind of hustle play...

857
00:40:26,844 --> 00:40:28,579
- is what wins us points.
- Right!

858
00:40:28,579 --> 00:40:32,016
It's a play that can create momentum
worth more than a point.

859
00:40:32,016 --> 00:40:33,251
That's right.

860
00:40:33,966 --> 00:40:36,835
The Wonder Dogs take the lead
with impressive defense.

861
00:40:37,115 --> 00:40:39,184
(Assigning target serve)

862
00:40:39,751 --> 00:40:42,187
(Target zone)

863
00:40:49,834 --> 00:40:51,702
Service ace!

864
00:40:53,405 --> 00:40:55,807
(The target serve tactic
worked perfectly.)

865
00:40:56,113 --> 00:40:57,842
- Nice!
- Nice!

866
00:40:58,383 --> 00:41:01,405
Looking back at the highlights
from the first set,

867
00:41:01,406 --> 00:41:04,902
Seung Ju scored big with her serve.

868
00:41:05,224 --> 00:41:07,159
Yun Ju has great attacking ability,

869
00:41:07,159 --> 00:41:09,728
but she does have a bit of a weak spot
when it comes to receiving.

870
00:41:10,496 --> 00:41:12,231
Yun Ju is feeling the pressure.

871
00:41:12,231 --> 00:41:13,149
(Aiming for Yun Ju with serves)

872
00:41:14,468 --> 00:41:16,470
(Seung Ju serving again)

873
00:41:16,670 --> 00:41:18,255
(Same zone again)

874
00:41:18,538 --> 00:41:20,173
(Targeting the same zone)

875
00:41:20,340 --> 00:41:22,075
(The target is, again, Yun Ju.)

876
00:41:22,643 --> 00:41:24,878
(Target confirmed.)

877
00:41:28,749 --> 00:41:29,650
Oh, no!

878
00:41:30,918 --> 00:41:32,219
(Hits the target)

879
00:41:35,022 --> 00:41:36,790
Another point off the serve!

880
00:41:38,191 --> 00:41:40,060
(That's all me.)

881
00:41:40,460 --> 00:41:42,429
(Service tactic worked perfectly.)

882
00:41:43,797 --> 00:41:47,801
(Bombastic! I like that play!)

883
00:41:47,801 --> 00:41:49,369
- Pyo Seung Ju!
- Pyo Seung Ju!

884
00:41:50,304 --> 00:41:52,339
(Calling a timeout)

885
00:41:52,623 --> 00:41:55,475
(Pink Spiders' timeout request)

886
00:41:56,007 --> 00:41:58,076
I'll break it down for you.
When Seung Ju is serving,

887
00:41:59,177 --> 00:42:01,279
Yun Ju stays here,
and Eun Ji, you step in.

888
00:42:01,646 --> 00:42:03,014
If they hit here, just stick with Eun Ji.

889
00:42:03,014 --> 00:42:05,250
If you stay together,
it would be hard to aim here.

890
00:42:05,250 --> 00:42:07,519
- Keep an eye on this area, got it?
- Okay.

891
00:42:07,519 --> 00:42:08,420
I'll keep an eye on it.

892
00:42:08,420 --> 00:42:12,102
They're trying to minimize
Yun Ju's reception coverage...

893
00:42:12,103 --> 00:42:15,299
and get her to focus more on her attacks.

894
00:42:15,666 --> 00:42:17,429
It's 1 to 4,
with a three-point difference.

895
00:42:17,889 --> 00:42:20,258
Wonder Dogs have taken the early lead.

896
00:42:20,258 --> 00:42:21,372
(Seung Ju's third service in a row)

897
00:42:23,862 --> 00:42:24,963
Aiming for Yun Ju again.

898
00:42:25,297 --> 00:42:26,098
Get it!

899
00:42:26,098 --> 00:42:28,279
(Barely receives it and tips over)

900
00:42:28,900 --> 00:42:30,001
They tip it over in a rush.

901
00:42:30,268 --> 00:42:31,336
It's a free ball.

902
00:42:31,636 --> 00:42:33,638
Here comes Enkhsoyol sprinting!

903
00:42:35,874 --> 00:42:37,309
Enkhsoyol!

904
00:42:38,076 --> 00:42:39,344
Spike with great power!

905
00:42:40,432 --> 00:42:41,967
(Unbelievably amazing!)

906
00:42:42,627 --> 00:42:44,295
Pink Spiders actually...

907
00:42:44,295 --> 00:42:47,064
made Yun Ju stick to the edge
of the line...

908
00:42:47,065 --> 00:42:50,102
and narrowed down her receiving range.

909
00:42:50,102 --> 00:42:53,371
But Seung Ju amazingly served...

910
00:42:53,371 --> 00:42:54,973
right in front of her.

911
00:42:57,742 --> 00:43:00,611
We have to ride this momentum.

912
00:43:01,813 --> 00:43:03,715
(Service to Yun Ju again)

913
00:43:03,715 --> 00:43:05,483
(But they save it and spike.)

914
00:43:05,483 --> 00:43:06,451
Yun Ju.

915
00:43:06,718 --> 00:43:08,653
Hye In sets it up high.

916
00:43:09,621 --> 00:43:10,889
Let's go!

917
00:43:12,157 --> 00:43:13,525
(Enkhsoyol's spike)

918
00:43:14,593 --> 00:43:15,813
That was a bit too long.

919
00:43:16,123 --> 00:43:18,792
Enkhsoyol overpowered that one.

920
00:43:19,126 --> 00:43:22,296
Wonder Dogs give the momentum back
with an attack error.

921
00:43:22,888 --> 00:43:25,109
(Pink Spiders serving now)

922
00:43:26,299 --> 00:43:27,533
It's a strong service.

923
00:43:29,336 --> 00:43:32,772
(The ball is set way too high.)

924
00:43:32,772 --> 00:43:34,340
It's too long. It's going over!

925
00:43:34,341 --> 00:43:35,309
(The ball goes over.)

926
00:43:36,643 --> 00:43:38,178
Pick it up and set it.

927
00:43:40,304 --> 00:43:42,416
(The ball is going
into the opponent's court?)

928
00:43:42,649 --> 00:43:43,516
Oh, no.

929
00:43:43,784 --> 00:43:46,253
The second-ball connection goes back over
to the other side again!

930
00:43:47,220 --> 00:43:48,521
(They get the ball...)

931
00:43:48,522 --> 00:43:49,690
(and spike!)

932
00:43:50,157 --> 00:43:51,425
They hit it right away.

933
00:43:52,392 --> 00:43:53,860
You have to look out for errors.

934
00:43:53,860 --> 00:43:55,706
(Consecutive connection errors)

935
00:43:55,896 --> 00:43:58,332
Hye In, how did I tell you
to set the service ball?

936
00:43:58,565 --> 00:43:59,432
Up.

937
00:43:59,866 --> 00:44:02,669
They lost a point
because of Hye In's connection error.

938
00:44:03,074 --> 00:44:04,642
(The match continues)

939
00:44:10,047 --> 00:44:11,181
(The ball is too close to the net.)

940
00:44:11,596 --> 00:44:13,465
The toss is too tight to the net.

941
00:44:15,273 --> 00:44:16,507
(Tried to tip it over,)

942
00:44:16,507 --> 00:44:18,476
(but failed.)

943
00:44:19,410 --> 00:44:20,244
Sorry.

944
00:44:22,087 --> 00:44:22,914
Na Yeon!

945
00:44:23,214 --> 00:44:25,009
There's no way they can hit that.

946
00:44:25,050 --> 00:44:26,285
Improve your setting accuracy!

947
00:44:27,594 --> 00:44:29,920
(Na Yeon is a bit shaky right now.)

948
00:44:30,226 --> 00:44:31,422
(Pink Spiders 4 : Wonder Dogs 5)

949
00:44:31,423 --> 00:44:34,593
It is now 5 to 4. The Wonder Dogs' lead is
down to one.

950
00:44:34,593 --> 00:44:36,328
(The opponents are
breathing down their necks.)

951
00:44:37,295 --> 00:44:39,296
(The service queen is on the job.)

952
00:44:41,299 --> 00:44:42,867
(A service error)

953
00:44:43,087 --> 00:44:43,821
It wasn't in?

954
00:44:44,388 --> 00:44:45,823
It's an error!

955
00:44:45,823 --> 00:44:46,563
(Of course, it was out!)

956
00:44:48,159 --> 00:44:50,194
She lifts it up with an underpass,
and Enkhsoyol spikes.

957
00:44:52,730 --> 00:44:53,664
It's blocked.

958
00:44:53,664 --> 00:44:55,599
- Hit it long, Enkhsoyol.
- Okay.

959
00:44:56,127 --> 00:44:57,561
(Smiling)

960
00:44:58,356 --> 00:45:00,698
The second set is staying close again.

961
00:45:00,778 --> 00:45:02,946
If the Wonder Dogs start to widen the gap,

962
00:45:02,946 --> 00:45:05,549
- the Pink Spiders are right on them.
- Right.

963
00:45:07,217 --> 00:45:08,785
They need to widen the gap.

964
00:45:12,456 --> 00:45:14,058
Hit it!

965
00:45:15,694 --> 00:45:16,807
(Tossing it back for...)

966
00:45:16,821 --> 00:45:18,349
(a back attack)

967
00:45:18,462 --> 00:45:19,763
Seung Ju's back attack!

968
00:45:20,998 --> 00:45:24,502
(The offense and defense keep
switching nonstop.)

969
00:45:25,602 --> 00:45:27,204
(Come on, break through!)

970
00:45:28,472 --> 00:45:29,439
(No way.)
Yun Ju, come on.

971
00:45:30,841 --> 00:45:31,975
Yun Ju's back attack!

972
00:45:33,277 --> 00:45:34,378
Song Hee digs it up!

973
00:45:39,083 --> 00:45:40,251
Get in!

974
00:45:40,751 --> 00:45:41,618
Cover me!

975
00:45:41,618 --> 00:45:43,053
(Eun Ji jumping up fiercely)

976
00:45:43,353 --> 00:45:44,888
(Wonder Dogs run over to defend,)

977
00:45:45,309 --> 00:45:47,357
(but Na Yeon put her hands down.)

978
00:45:47,357 --> 00:45:48,191
Hit it!

979
00:45:49,326 --> 00:45:50,193
Hit it!

980
00:45:50,194 --> 00:45:52,096
(Lost a point)

981
00:45:52,496 --> 00:45:54,331
Why did you pull down? Why?

982
00:45:55,432 --> 00:45:57,334
She was hoping for an out,

983
00:45:57,668 --> 00:45:59,036
but the ball dropped in.

984
00:45:59,803 --> 00:46:02,405
- Why did you pull back?
- I thought it was out.

985
00:46:02,406 --> 00:46:04,882
The Wonder Dogs can't seem to pull ahead.

986
00:46:04,883 --> 00:46:05,909
(Pink Spiders 7 : Wonder Dogs 9)

987
00:46:06,643 --> 00:46:07,944
They're substituting the setter.

988
00:46:08,712 --> 00:46:11,715
(Na Yeon out, Jin in)

989
00:46:12,222 --> 00:46:12,850
(Thinking)

990
00:46:12,850 --> 00:46:14,918
They're substituting the setter.
Jin is in now.

991
00:46:14,918 --> 00:46:16,586
Song Hee!

992
00:46:17,528 --> 00:46:20,157
(Set quick to Hyeon Jeong)

993
00:46:20,157 --> 00:46:21,792
- Watch out for short service!
- Hyeon Jeong, run.

994
00:46:22,053 --> 00:46:23,694
(Okay, got it.)

995
00:46:23,694 --> 00:46:25,462
Now that setter Jin is on the court,

996
00:46:25,462 --> 00:46:27,497
will they be able to regain the momentum?

997
00:46:28,098 --> 00:46:29,800
- Short serve, Hyeon Jeong.
- It's 9 to 7.

998
00:46:29,800 --> 00:46:30,834
Da Sol is serving.

999
00:46:32,369 --> 00:46:33,203
Hye In.

1000
00:46:33,403 --> 00:46:34,404
Jin.

1001
00:46:34,404 --> 00:46:35,338
(Back toss to Hyeon Jeong)

1002
00:46:35,338 --> 00:46:36,406
Hyeon Jeong is running!

1003
00:46:36,907 --> 00:46:37,808
A slide attack!

1004
00:46:39,143 --> 00:46:41,211
Point off the block!

1005
00:46:41,211 --> 00:46:42,512
(Successful point off the block)

1006
00:46:42,586 --> 00:46:44,067
(Great job.)

1007
00:46:44,275 --> 00:46:47,211
(Nice combination play!)

1008
00:46:48,005 --> 00:46:50,874
The newly-subbed player is
lifting their spirits.

1009
00:46:50,875 --> 00:46:51,776
Indeed.

1010
00:46:51,776 --> 00:46:53,511
(Sliding over)

1011
00:46:53,511 --> 00:46:54,412
Jin.

1012
00:46:54,432 --> 00:46:56,340
(Calling Jin again)

1013
00:46:56,814 --> 00:47:01,018
(Set it so that the left can
aim for Zone Six.)

1014
00:47:01,419 --> 00:47:02,219
Back again.

1015
00:47:02,219 --> 00:47:04,788
They just have to ride the momentum
as they are now.

1016
00:47:04,956 --> 00:47:08,567
Coach Yeon Koung is trying
to shift the flow by using setter Jin.

1017
00:47:08,574 --> 00:47:09,586
(Ready to take a step back again)

1018
00:47:09,607 --> 00:47:11,442
(The match continues.)

1019
00:47:11,896 --> 00:47:12,696
Jin.

1020
00:47:12,696 --> 00:47:14,264
(Setting it to Seung Ju)

1021
00:47:14,365 --> 00:47:15,232
She tips!

1022
00:47:15,700 --> 00:47:17,602
Da Sol receives it.

1023
00:47:18,135 --> 00:47:18,969
Yun Ju.
(Yun Ju's counterattack)

1024
00:47:19,904 --> 00:47:20,938
It's saved.

1025
00:47:20,938 --> 00:47:22,106
(The ball is set for Seung Ju again.)

1026
00:47:22,413 --> 00:47:24,849
(Coach Yeon Koung has been reinforcing...)

1027
00:47:25,183 --> 00:47:27,485
(the tactic of aiming
for Zone Six from set one.)

1028
00:47:27,652 --> 00:47:29,454
(Confirmed that Zone Six is empty.)

1029
00:47:29,747 --> 00:47:30,547
Hit it!

1030
00:47:30,547 --> 00:47:32,549
(Tossed it to Seung Ju right away.)

1031
00:47:33,918 --> 00:47:36,020
- Seung Ju!
- Yes!

1032
00:47:36,020 --> 00:47:37,087
Point off the block!

1033
00:47:37,087 --> 00:47:38,162
(Converting it into a point)

1034
00:47:38,436 --> 00:47:39,837
(Not happy about this situation)

1035
00:47:40,204 --> 00:47:42,740
(The Wonder Dogs are coming alive again!)

1036
00:47:43,034 --> 00:47:45,470
That was a great connection play.

1037
00:47:45,650 --> 00:47:47,285
Jin!

1038
00:47:47,885 --> 00:47:49,854
(Thumbs up for Jin)

1039
00:47:49,854 --> 00:47:52,223
A play that shows
perfect understanding of the game's flow.

1040
00:47:52,451 --> 00:47:54,386
The atmosphere of the Wonder Dogs is
coming alive!

1041
00:47:55,226 --> 00:47:56,527
The score is 12 to 8.

1042
00:47:56,694 --> 00:47:58,829
We're leading by four points.

1043
00:48:01,166 --> 00:48:02,600
Jin! Open it!

1044
00:48:02,600 --> 00:48:03,835
(Get in your blocking position)

1045
00:48:03,835 --> 00:48:05,236
Watch out for Yun Ju's timing.

1046
00:48:06,237 --> 00:48:08,472
They need to keep Yun Ju in check.

1047
00:48:08,540 --> 00:48:10,475
(We need to contain Yun Ju.)

1048
00:48:10,475 --> 00:48:12,076
(Hyeon Jeong's service)

1049
00:48:13,178 --> 00:48:14,546
Su Been barely receives it.

1050
00:48:15,213 --> 00:48:16,847
(Yun Ju getting ready to attack)

1051
00:48:17,167 --> 00:48:20,664
(The key is to jump
at the right timing for blocking.)

1052
00:48:24,989 --> 00:48:27,425
Yun Ju scores off the block.

1053
00:48:27,871 --> 00:48:29,246
- Good.
- Push the ball to Yun Ju.

1054
00:48:29,260 --> 00:48:30,695
Yun Ju really is a strong opponent.

1055
00:48:30,929 --> 00:48:33,598
Yun Ju is shaking things up once again.

1056
00:48:34,098 --> 00:48:35,515
Look out for tips!

1057
00:48:35,515 --> 00:48:37,283
(The continuing brilliance of Yun Ju)

1058
00:48:38,122 --> 00:48:39,218
Spike.

1059
00:48:40,420 --> 00:48:41,788
(A barely made dig)

1060
00:48:42,897 --> 00:48:44,957
- They made the dig. Jin.
- Nice save.

1061
00:48:45,290 --> 00:48:46,377
- Seung Ju!
- Yes!

1062
00:48:46,657 --> 00:48:48,394
Yun Ju might hit it short.

1063
00:48:48,710 --> 00:48:49,962
It's Yun Ju once again.

1064
00:48:51,481 --> 00:48:53,133
(While hesitating,)

1065
00:48:55,068 --> 00:48:57,187
(is their defense cracking?)

1066
00:48:58,315 --> 00:48:59,016
(Flying down)

1067
00:48:59,036 --> 00:49:02,075
- It's a push-in point.
- That was perfectly placed.

1068
00:49:02,320 --> 00:49:03,520
Yun Ju, nice job.

1069
00:49:03,553 --> 00:49:05,553
They keep giving Yun Ju the points.

1070
00:49:06,199 --> 00:49:07,926
Where were you going?

1071
00:49:08,493 --> 00:49:10,380
(They couldn't build a wall.)

1072
00:49:10,531 --> 00:49:13,136
It's better to block the right side.
One blocking is enough over there.

1073
00:49:13,451 --> 00:49:17,137
Song Hee is there to cover.
This is really frustrating.

1074
00:49:18,437 --> 00:49:22,493
Myoung Hwa failed to join the block.

1075
00:49:22,499 --> 00:49:24,261
And immediately,
the coach gave a sharp critique.

1076
00:49:25,097 --> 00:49:29,600
(In the end, she pulls
out the substitution card.)

1077
00:49:30,179 --> 00:49:32,369
Young In is on the court.

1078
00:49:32,370 --> 00:49:35,272
(Young In in, Song Hee out)

1079
00:49:35,963 --> 00:49:38,208
(Time to restore
Quick Myoung Hwa's pride...)

1080
00:49:38,469 --> 00:49:40,938
(with a serve.)

1081
00:49:41,269 --> 00:49:43,071
(Show us what you've got, Myoung Hwa.)

1082
00:49:43,538 --> 00:49:45,206
(The serve ace's time)

1083
00:49:46,874 --> 00:49:48,142
(She shook up the opponent as expected!)

1084
00:49:49,349 --> 00:49:50,211
Net touch.

1085
00:49:50,711 --> 00:49:51,679
It's a net touch!

1086
00:49:52,280 --> 00:49:54,582
(The Wonder Dogs' net touch?)

1087
00:49:54,815 --> 00:49:56,383
Who did that?

1088
00:49:57,718 --> 00:50:01,555
(Everyone is puzzled.)

1089
00:50:01,635 --> 00:50:04,815
A net touch is called on the Wonder Dogs.

1090
00:50:09,641 --> 00:50:10,803
- Did you touch the net?
- No.

1091
00:50:12,900 --> 00:50:14,973
Did I? I didn't feel it at all.

1092
00:50:15,981 --> 00:50:18,862
(They all say they didn't touch the net.)

1093
00:50:19,196 --> 00:50:21,532
(The referee says
it was Hyeon Jeong's error.)

1094
00:50:22,640 --> 00:50:26,110
- Who was it?
- You did! So, did you touch the net?

1095
00:50:26,145 --> 00:50:27,678
No, I didn't, but my shirt could have.

1096
00:50:28,392 --> 00:50:29,681
She said no.

1097
00:50:30,764 --> 00:50:33,718
The Wonder Dogs have requested
a video review for the net touch.

1098
00:50:34,184 --> 00:50:37,118
Don't talk to the referee. Talk to me.

1099
00:50:37,119 --> 00:50:38,268
Or I can't request a video review.

1100
00:50:38,269 --> 00:50:39,996
- Did you touch it or not?
- Not with my arms.

1101
00:50:40,203 --> 00:50:44,295
It seems like Hyeon Jeong is not
sure about it.

1102
00:50:44,449 --> 00:50:46,106
(Look at her face.)

1103
00:50:46,423 --> 00:50:48,518
Yeon Koung asked if she touched it or not.

1104
00:50:48,519 --> 00:50:51,790
- That's right.
- But she's not so sure about it.

1105
00:50:52,569 --> 00:50:55,326
Why did you touch the net?
And did you touch it or not?

1106
00:50:55,754 --> 00:50:57,528
I didn't feel it at all.

1107
00:50:58,094 --> 00:51:00,094
So, you didn't touch it.
You'd better hope so.

1108
00:51:00,832 --> 00:51:03,568
(That's such a terrifying joke.)

1109
00:51:04,168 --> 00:51:06,437
(The video review is underway.)

1110
00:51:07,639 --> 00:51:09,541
(I trust you, Hyeon Jeong.)

1111
00:51:13,478 --> 00:51:17,415
(Her hands did not touch the net.)

1112
00:51:18,149 --> 00:51:21,519
(If she didn't touch it with her shirt,
it's not a foul.)

1113
00:51:22,787 --> 00:51:24,555
(But it did.)

1114
00:51:25,342 --> 00:51:26,943
Myoung Hwa, nice serve.

1115
00:51:26,991 --> 00:51:28,826
It's ruled a net touch.

1116
00:51:28,860 --> 00:51:29,828
(Seriously?)

1117
00:51:30,328 --> 00:51:32,135
(Pale)

1118
00:51:32,363 --> 00:51:33,998
Oh, my.

1119
00:51:36,134 --> 00:51:39,404
(Her shirt brushed the net so lightly
that she didn't feel it.)

1120
00:51:39,625 --> 00:51:40,805
My arm touched it?

1121
00:51:41,839 --> 00:51:44,818
Hyeon Jeong didn't feel it.

1122
00:51:44,830 --> 00:51:46,844
- It was too light to feel.
- Right.

1123
00:51:47,024 --> 00:51:51,749
During the game, players sometimes touch
the net without even realizing it.

1124
00:51:53,450 --> 00:51:56,921
The second technical timeout of Set Two
starts with a score of 16 to 12.

1125
00:51:58,176 --> 00:52:00,303
- You said you didn't touch it.
- Right.

1126
00:52:01,075 --> 00:52:03,013
Does it not count
if only your arm doesn't touch?

1127
00:52:03,034 --> 00:52:03,553
No.

1128
00:52:03,568 --> 00:52:05,930
- You should've told me honestly.
- I didn't feel it. Okay.

1129
00:52:06,600 --> 00:52:08,391
- "Okay."
- "Okay."

1130
00:52:08,607 --> 00:52:11,402
Coach Kim has also done this a lot...

1131
00:52:11,403 --> 00:52:13,871
during her athletic career.

1132
00:52:15,539 --> 00:52:18,398
Maybe they'll keep talking about this...

1133
00:52:18,797 --> 00:52:21,666
- today, even after the game.
- Of course.

1134
00:52:22,868 --> 00:52:24,537
Handle the attacks a bit better.

1135
00:52:24,538 --> 00:52:26,905
And time your blocks well.
You can wait a little longer...

1136
00:52:27,197 --> 00:52:30,142
because their contact point is a bit low.

1137
00:52:30,167 --> 00:52:32,189
(The Pink Spiders attack
from a relatively lower point,)

1138
00:52:32,662 --> 00:52:36,213
(so their hit timing comes
a bit later than other teams.)

1139
00:52:36,586 --> 00:52:38,589
(Catching on)

1140
00:52:38,863 --> 00:52:40,161
If you jump too early,

1141
00:52:40,810 --> 00:52:41,810
it could lead to a block-out,

1142
00:52:42,703 --> 00:52:44,703
so wait a bit before jumping.

1143
00:52:45,359 --> 00:52:46,855
Just slightly delay your jump timing.

1144
00:52:50,168 --> 00:52:51,088
- Yes, Coach.
- Yes, Coach!

1145
00:52:51,336 --> 00:52:52,916
Let's do this!

1146
00:52:53,424 --> 00:52:54,158
You got this!

1147
00:52:54,365 --> 00:52:55,465
We got this!

1148
00:52:56,293 --> 00:52:58,179
Just pay a little more attention
to blocking.

1149
00:52:58,546 --> 00:53:01,649
Don't miss the easy ones,
and let's give it our best.

1150
00:53:03,113 --> 00:53:04,728
Let's go!

1151
00:53:04,782 --> 00:53:06,370
(In this fierce blocking battle,)

1152
00:53:07,871 --> 00:53:10,480
(who will be victorious?)

1153
00:53:11,702 --> 00:53:15,149
(A serve by Young In)

1154
00:53:16,640 --> 00:53:17,793
Eun Ji receives it.

1155
00:53:21,173 --> 00:53:22,698
Their contact point is a bit low.

1156
00:53:23,332 --> 00:53:24,800
(I have to make up for...)

1157
00:53:24,959 --> 00:53:26,368
Just slightly delay your jump timing.

1158
00:53:26,931 --> 00:53:28,666
(my error with this!)

1159
00:53:30,168 --> 00:53:32,270
(Perfectly calculated timing)

1160
00:53:32,346 --> 00:53:35,891
- Nice block!
- Hyeon Jeong made a good block.

1161
00:53:35,892 --> 00:53:37,809
(A perfect block)

1162
00:53:42,206 --> 00:53:45,779
Now, we all must erase
her net touch mistake...

1163
00:53:45,785 --> 00:53:47,505
from our heads.

1164
00:53:47,506 --> 00:53:50,909
Hyeon Jeong has
completely made up for the error.

1165
00:53:54,012 --> 00:53:57,249
(A minor net touch error can be...)

1166
00:53:58,691 --> 00:54:01,294
(covered with a good block.)

1167
00:54:01,312 --> 00:54:04,115
(You are forgiven.)

1168
00:54:04,949 --> 00:54:07,718
(The momentum is fully restored.)

1169
00:54:10,161 --> 00:54:12,248
Hye Jin.

1170
00:54:12,476 --> 00:54:13,483
Keep the left side covered...

1171
00:54:13,484 --> 00:54:15,138
- and try going with the pipe and back C.
- Okay.

1172
00:54:22,592 --> 00:54:25,722
(Young In serves again.)

1173
00:54:27,531 --> 00:54:28,531
Young In.

1174
00:54:29,693 --> 00:54:31,268
(A back C as planned)

1175
00:54:32,135 --> 00:54:35,405
(Is their block a step late?)

1176
00:54:36,331 --> 00:54:37,875
Jin digs it.

1177
00:54:38,842 --> 00:54:41,278
Nice job, Jin.

1178
00:54:43,480 --> 00:54:45,769
(Young In follows up
with a two-touch combination.)

1179
00:54:46,836 --> 00:54:49,412
(She's been emphasizing targeting
the space at Zone Six all along.)

1180
00:54:49,840 --> 00:54:50,627
(Yes, Coach.)

1181
00:54:55,434 --> 00:54:59,196
- Enkhsoyol's high ball dink!
- That's incredible.

1182
00:54:59,568 --> 00:55:01,904
(Point successfully scored)

1183
00:55:10,080 --> 00:55:11,736
Yun Ju, prepare for a pipe.

1184
00:55:15,133 --> 00:55:17,676
Hye In, watch where the ball is going.

1185
00:55:26,031 --> 00:55:27,431
(Going for the pipe)

1186
00:55:27,571 --> 00:55:28,972
A back attack from the back row.

1187
00:55:28,973 --> 00:55:31,141
(I must save it.)

1188
00:55:32,248 --> 00:55:33,248
They defend it.

1189
00:55:33,249 --> 00:55:34,097
(Hye In solidly defends)

1190
00:55:35,534 --> 00:55:37,381
Jin sets it up.

1191
00:55:37,382 --> 00:55:39,823
(And it goes to Enkhsoyol again.)

1192
00:55:42,066 --> 00:55:45,422
A spike by Enkhsoyol!

1193
00:55:46,456 --> 00:55:48,024
The Wonder Dogs score two points in a row.

1194
00:55:48,712 --> 00:55:50,742
(Two points in a row from Zone Six)

1195
00:55:51,054 --> 00:55:54,591
They score from Zone Six,
which the coach has been emphasizing!

1196
00:55:55,654 --> 00:55:58,856
The Wonder Dogs are leading
by seven points.

1197
00:55:58,857 --> 00:56:00,324
(We've got the momentum now!)

1198
00:56:00,858 --> 00:56:02,993
(The match continues.)

1199
00:56:04,895 --> 00:56:05,768
(Powerful Seung Ju)

1200
00:56:05,768 --> 00:56:06,969
Seung Ju!

1201
00:56:06,970 --> 00:56:09,266
A perfectly executed cross-court spike!

1202
00:56:13,037 --> 00:56:14,672
(During the next rally,)

1203
00:56:16,460 --> 00:56:17,668
Seung Ju!

1204
00:56:17,669 --> 00:56:20,310
(she shot it in
with a down-the-line attack.)

1205
00:56:21,554 --> 00:56:23,347
The Wonder Dogs are in perfect sync.

1206
00:56:23,348 --> 00:56:25,249
(Second set, Pink Spiders 15
: Wonder Dogs 23)

1207
00:56:26,417 --> 00:56:28,719
(The Wonder Dogs keep attacking.)

1208
00:56:29,384 --> 00:56:30,588
Toward Enkhsoyol!

1209
00:56:33,424 --> 00:56:35,972
(Seung Ju's left-side cross-court spike)

1210
00:56:35,999 --> 00:56:37,026
It goes over.

1211
00:56:37,588 --> 00:56:38,421
Jin!

1212
00:56:41,012 --> 00:56:43,147
(Where will it be heading
over to this time?)

1213
00:56:44,315 --> 00:56:46,217
(In a muddle)

1214
00:56:46,818 --> 00:56:47,519
(A back attack!)

1215
00:56:52,195 --> 00:56:55,371
(They targeted Zone Six once again.)

1216
00:56:55,680 --> 00:56:56,662
(Screaming)

1217
00:56:56,662 --> 00:56:58,062
What a successful attack!

1218
00:57:00,231 --> 00:57:02,533
(Satisfied)

1219
00:57:03,268 --> 00:57:06,138
(Enkhsoyol perfectly executed
the strategy.)

1220
00:57:07,450 --> 00:57:09,578
The Wonder Dogs reach set point
in the second set.

1221
00:57:10,642 --> 00:57:12,611
(Second set, Pink Spiders 19
: Wonder Dogs 24)

1222
00:57:12,705 --> 00:57:16,213
Just one more point,
and they can take the second set.

1223
00:57:16,214 --> 00:57:17,854
Just one more!

1224
00:57:17,915 --> 00:57:18,921
Jin, don't hesitate.

1225
00:57:23,447 --> 00:57:25,114
Han Song Hee and Lee Jin!

1226
00:57:25,481 --> 00:57:27,581
They didn't prepare to attack.

1227
00:57:27,581 --> 00:57:28,585
(An easy chance to attack missed)

1228
00:57:30,514 --> 00:57:31,881
(The Pink Spiders' quick shot
in the middle)

1229
00:57:32,081 --> 00:57:33,447
She hit it to the back.

1230
00:57:33,481 --> 00:57:34,814
They defended it.

1231
00:57:40,381 --> 00:57:42,014
Seung Ju spikes!

1232
00:57:42,547 --> 00:57:44,181
She scores!

1233
00:57:45,547 --> 00:57:48,214
Seung Ju finishes the set.

1234
00:57:50,814 --> 00:57:52,981
So it ends 25 to 19.

1235
00:57:53,781 --> 00:57:56,414
The Wonder Dogs win
the second set as well.

1236
00:57:58,842 --> 00:58:00,375
(Timeout for the third set)

1237
00:58:00,911 --> 00:58:03,644
You remember the third set in Japan?

1238
00:58:03,644 --> 00:58:04,644
Yes.

1239
00:58:05,523 --> 00:58:08,338
(Even though they won two sets,)

1240
00:58:09,685 --> 00:58:13,735
(they lost three sets by a comeback
from the other team.)

1241
00:58:15,692 --> 00:58:17,259
- Don't think about it again.
- Yes, Coach.

1242
00:58:17,292 --> 00:58:20,026
Focus right from the start.

1243
00:58:20,092 --> 00:58:21,259
- Yes!
- Let's go!

1244
00:58:21,359 --> 00:58:25,059
- Know that many errors are from tips.
- Okay!

1245
00:58:25,092 --> 00:58:27,192
Don't just stand around.
Send signals verbally...

1246
00:58:27,192 --> 00:58:29,526
- on what you'll do.
- Yes.

1247
00:58:30,974 --> 00:58:33,174
(Meanwhile, the Pink Spiders' timeout)

1248
00:58:36,814 --> 00:58:40,580
- For this set...
- We need to do it properly.

1249
00:58:41,147 --> 00:58:42,614
We can't lose 3 to 0.

1250
00:58:43,847 --> 00:58:45,780
(Due to the Wonder Dogs'
unexpected force,)

1251
00:58:45,814 --> 00:58:49,847
We try to give up on quick hits,
but it's meaningless when you're late.

1252
00:58:49,914 --> 00:58:51,714
(the Pink Spiders are flustered.)

1253
00:58:52,914 --> 00:58:57,880
(All the setters' tosses go left.)

1254
00:58:57,880 --> 00:58:59,280
After receiving?

1255
00:59:00,080 --> 00:59:01,480
Listen.

1256
00:59:01,480 --> 00:59:03,847
Don't fly off when you block right.
Just close the gap.

1257
00:59:03,847 --> 00:59:06,614
Defenders in Zone Four watch here.

1258
00:59:06,614 --> 00:59:08,780
And Zone One defenders shouldn't move
too far and stay around here.

1259
00:59:08,780 --> 00:59:09,847
Yes!

1260
00:59:11,114 --> 00:59:15,447
(Let's win the third set!)

1261
00:59:16,014 --> 00:59:21,647
The Wonder Dogs won two sets
against the Pink Spiders, the champions.

1262
00:59:22,105 --> 00:59:25,719
Yes. In the second set, Seung Ju
and Enkhsoyol's double hits are...

1263
00:59:25,747 --> 00:59:28,280
were in perfect sync.

1264
00:59:29,353 --> 00:59:32,019
(The Wonder Dogs are on a roll.)

1265
00:59:32,619 --> 00:59:35,353
(If they win this set,)

1266
00:59:35,953 --> 00:59:38,486
(the match will be over
with a shutout victory.)

1267
00:59:38,986 --> 00:59:41,193
(The third set will clearly be
a turning point.)

1268
00:59:41,698 --> 00:59:42,898
The third set starts.

1269
00:59:42,898 --> 00:59:43,954
(Park Min Ji serves.)

1270
00:59:45,965 --> 00:59:47,098
- Nice reception.
- Mine!

1271
00:59:51,065 --> 00:59:52,495
(Song Hee rushes in.)

1272
00:59:52,898 --> 00:59:55,332
Don't fly off when you block right.
Just close the gap.

1273
00:59:55,332 --> 00:59:56,365
(Mark the right side.)

1274
00:59:56,365 --> 00:59:57,832
Watch it!

1275
00:59:58,332 --> 00:59:59,398
Spike!

1276
01:00:00,098 --> 01:00:01,232
They saved it.

1277
01:00:02,265 --> 01:00:04,565
It's a rebound play. One more time!

1278
01:00:05,465 --> 01:00:06,965
Song Hee spikes!

1279
01:00:07,432 --> 01:00:09,265
Min Ji throws her body.

1280
01:00:09,632 --> 01:00:11,732
Slow down!

1281
01:00:13,798 --> 01:00:15,065
Yun Ju.

1282
01:00:15,698 --> 01:00:17,365
Hye In digs.

1283
01:00:19,782 --> 01:00:21,098
(The little giant rises.)

1284
01:00:23,998 --> 01:00:25,465
In 1, 2, 3!

1285
01:00:26,132 --> 01:00:27,798
- It's blocked.
- Well.

1286
01:00:27,798 --> 01:00:29,132
(The right side is completely blocked.)

1287
01:00:31,465 --> 01:00:32,932
Let's go!

1288
01:00:33,665 --> 01:00:35,465
- I'm sorry.
- It's fine.

1289
01:00:35,465 --> 01:00:36,873
(Their spike is totally blocked.)

1290
01:00:40,032 --> 01:00:42,132
Jin!

1291
01:00:42,432 --> 01:00:43,898
(Sending a sign)

1292
01:00:43,934 --> 01:00:45,348
(After receiving it,)

1293
01:00:46,100 --> 01:00:48,900
(she passes it to others.)

1294
01:00:49,334 --> 01:00:51,734
(Understood)

1295
01:00:52,667 --> 01:00:53,667
You got this!

1296
01:00:55,645 --> 01:00:57,234
Min Ji serves.

1297
01:00:58,700 --> 01:00:59,800
Hye In receives.

1298
01:00:59,800 --> 01:01:01,900
(Nice reception)

1299
01:01:02,534 --> 01:01:04,634
(A perfect time to toss)

1300
01:01:05,100 --> 01:01:06,900
(This is their chance!)

1301
01:01:07,400 --> 01:01:08,400
Lee Jin.

1302
01:01:08,400 --> 01:01:09,800
(Jin's quick toss)

1303
01:01:11,067 --> 01:01:12,834
Han Song Hee scores!

1304
01:01:12,834 --> 01:01:14,000
Nice toss!

1305
01:01:16,666 --> 01:01:18,367
Nice set up!

1306
01:01:18,749 --> 01:01:19,749
Jin!

1307
01:01:19,749 --> 01:01:21,449
(Was Lee Jin's quick toss
the rookie coach's strategy?)

1308
01:01:21,612 --> 01:01:23,319
(During the review meeting
before the match)

1309
01:01:23,749 --> 01:01:26,182
You know the turbo in a Porsche.

1310
01:01:26,549 --> 01:01:28,649
It's just like how turbos work.

1311
01:01:28,749 --> 01:01:32,035
If you shift into gear with a turbo,
it roars and takes off.

1312
01:01:32,882 --> 01:01:35,982
Just like that, they'll be quicker
if they use turbo.

1313
01:01:36,316 --> 01:01:40,749
We'll toss the ball faster
than the setter usually sets.

1314
01:01:40,782 --> 01:01:42,782
Let's give it a go.

1315
01:01:42,816 --> 01:01:46,282
When there's a free ball
or you receive it well,

1316
01:01:46,416 --> 01:01:49,049
you move in when there's a sign for turbo.

1317
01:01:52,742 --> 01:01:54,857
(A slightly faster play)

1318
01:01:55,405 --> 01:01:57,827
(It worked perfectly.)

1319
01:01:58,238 --> 01:02:01,170
(Flustered)

1320
01:02:05,021 --> 01:02:07,521
(Enkhsoyol is back to the left side.)

1321
01:02:08,221 --> 01:02:09,721
(But...)

1322
01:02:10,054 --> 01:02:12,321
(they surround her...)

1323
01:02:12,721 --> 01:02:15,471
(in perfect sync?)

1324
01:02:16,121 --> 01:02:19,621
When Enkhsoyol's ball is high,
check when she jumps.

1325
01:02:19,621 --> 01:02:21,588
- Then you leap to block. Okay?
- Yes, Coach.

1326
01:02:22,906 --> 01:02:26,821
(They begin to focus on Enkhsoyol.)

1327
01:02:32,015 --> 01:02:33,281
Seung Ju serves.

1328
01:02:35,648 --> 01:02:37,181
Pyo Seung Ju!

1329
01:02:39,415 --> 01:02:41,048
- Go!
- The reception is short.

1330
01:02:41,115 --> 01:02:42,881
Move in!

1331
01:02:42,881 --> 01:02:43,786
(Jeong Yun Ju's spike)
She hits hard.

1332
01:02:45,148 --> 01:02:46,881
It bounces after they block.

1333
01:02:46,881 --> 01:02:48,448
(It's the Wonder Dogs' chance to attack)

1334
01:02:49,081 --> 01:02:50,548
Nice toss!

1335
01:02:51,328 --> 01:02:53,481
(Enkhsoyol is ready.)

1336
01:02:53,648 --> 01:02:56,248
High ball! Slow down!

1337
01:02:57,948 --> 01:02:59,115
Spike!

1338
01:03:00,715 --> 01:03:03,281
It lands inside the court!

1339
01:03:05,902 --> 01:03:09,312
(Enkhsoyol's refreshing point...)

1340
01:03:09,313 --> 01:03:12,448
(that no one expected)

1341
01:03:13,415 --> 01:03:14,730
It's 2 to 2.

1342
01:03:14,731 --> 01:03:16,405
(Third set, Pink Spiders 2
: Wonder Dogs 2)

1343
01:03:17,015 --> 01:03:18,115
Hye Rim is the server.

1344
01:03:21,191 --> 01:03:22,925
(Glaring)

1345
01:03:24,434 --> 01:03:25,188
(Glancing)

1346
01:03:34,848 --> 01:03:36,381
Mine!

1347
01:03:36,381 --> 01:03:38,215
She saves the ball,
and it goes up quickly.

1348
01:03:38,315 --> 01:03:40,281
The set up was done in a hurry,
but they defended it.

1349
01:03:41,815 --> 01:03:43,248
Yun Ju spikes!

1350
01:03:44,334 --> 01:03:46,368
(Hye In digs.)

1351
01:03:46,768 --> 01:03:47,768
That's it.

1352
01:03:51,734 --> 01:03:54,568
Enkhsoyol spikes, but they defend it!

1353
01:03:55,668 --> 01:03:58,668
(The ball goes to Yun Ju again.)

1354
01:04:01,004 --> 01:04:02,237
Go!

1355
01:04:02,537 --> 01:04:04,804
Yun Ju spikes once more!

1356
01:04:06,237 --> 01:04:07,437
Sorry.

1357
01:04:12,704 --> 01:04:15,304
That was nice defense!

1358
01:04:17,871 --> 01:04:20,871
I played like a mad person.

1359
01:04:21,237 --> 01:04:25,937
I wanted to win at all costs
since it was our last match.

1360
01:04:25,971 --> 01:04:27,137
Enkhsoyol!

1361
01:04:27,137 --> 01:04:28,804
The ball will come here.

1362
01:04:28,804 --> 01:04:30,971
(Two hitters' head-to-head battle)

1363
01:04:31,137 --> 01:04:32,281
It's 2 to 4.

1364
01:04:32,282 --> 01:04:33,637
(Third set, Pink Spiders 4
: Wonder Dogs 2)

1365
01:04:35,965 --> 01:04:37,370
Seung Ju receives it.

1366
01:04:37,371 --> 01:04:38,214
Now to Jin.

1367
01:04:38,215 --> 01:04:39,604
(Tossing to Enkhsoyol)

1368
01:04:43,804 --> 01:04:45,771
(Immediately getting ready for a spike)

1369
01:04:46,237 --> 01:04:50,437
(With all her might,)

1370
01:04:50,437 --> 01:04:53,271
(she tips?)

1371
01:04:59,771 --> 01:05:01,737
Nice!

1372
01:05:02,671 --> 01:05:05,037
- That was to Zone 3.
- Zone 3!

1373
01:05:07,745 --> 01:05:10,878
(Enkhsoyol is nailing the game.)

1374
01:05:12,011 --> 01:05:14,511
(And Yun Ju is full of determination.)

1375
01:05:15,211 --> 01:05:17,045
(After strengthening her reception)

1376
01:05:17,111 --> 01:05:18,111
Yun Ju!

1377
01:05:20,578 --> 01:05:22,811
- She scores!
- That was a nice hitting point.

1378
01:05:22,911 --> 01:05:24,778
- Nice!
- Okay!

1379
01:05:25,721 --> 01:05:26,745
Come on.

1380
01:05:27,511 --> 01:05:28,778
(We block Yun Ju's hits...)

1381
01:05:29,678 --> 01:05:32,045
Enkhsoyol scores with a blockout!

1382
01:05:32,078 --> 01:05:34,537
(with Enkhsoyol.)

1383
01:05:34,945 --> 01:05:38,845
(The two teams' battle
of attacks is intense.)

1384
01:05:40,169 --> 01:05:41,478
Song Hee serves.

1385
01:05:43,513 --> 01:05:45,611
(Instructing the target area to serve)

1386
01:05:57,527 --> 01:05:59,678
Run!

1387
01:06:00,450 --> 01:06:02,203
A service ace!

1388
01:06:02,204 --> 01:06:03,578
Nice, Song Hee!

1389
01:06:07,811 --> 01:06:10,245
(It's a point!)

1390
01:06:10,845 --> 01:06:13,245
(Speechless)

1391
01:06:15,431 --> 01:06:16,678
- One more point!
- Yes!

1392
01:06:16,678 --> 01:06:19,045
(Third set, Pink Spiders 7: Wonder Dogs 7)

1393
01:06:20,145 --> 01:06:23,245
(We'll take back the lead like this.)

1394
01:06:23,599 --> 01:06:24,711
Yun Ju, look out for quicks!

1395
01:06:29,378 --> 01:06:30,478
Seung Ju receives.

1396
01:06:30,745 --> 01:06:33,611
She gets the ball and pushes in.
There's coverage for her.

1397
01:06:33,944 --> 01:06:34,678
Seung Ju!

1398
01:06:34,678 --> 01:06:36,578
(Their opportunity to attack again)

1399
01:06:37,578 --> 01:06:39,081
(It's our chance!)

1400
01:06:40,062 --> 01:06:41,411
Send it long.

1401
01:06:45,745 --> 01:06:46,745
(Touched)

1402
01:06:46,823 --> 01:06:48,078
She touched it!

1403
01:06:48,445 --> 01:06:51,787
Seung Ju spikes, and she scores!

1404
01:06:51,788 --> 01:06:53,209
(A block-touch out)

1405
01:06:54,811 --> 01:06:56,944
(They turned the tables.)

1406
01:06:56,945 --> 01:06:59,978
It's 8 to 7, and the Wonder Dogs have
taken back the lead.

1407
01:06:59,978 --> 01:07:02,345
And we're now on a technical timeout.

1408
01:07:02,345 --> 01:07:03,478
(Technical timeout)

1409
01:07:03,478 --> 01:07:05,347
- You see the score?
- Yes.

1410
01:07:05,348 --> 01:07:07,335
We have a chance now.

1411
01:07:07,350 --> 01:07:09,611
- So we must secure it, okay?
- Understood.

1412
01:07:09,645 --> 01:07:11,039
Let's pump the vibes up.

1413
01:07:11,040 --> 01:07:12,911
Get more points!

1414
01:07:13,011 --> 01:07:15,345
- Block the sides well.
- Yes.

1415
01:07:15,645 --> 01:07:17,711
- Time it right with no gap.
- Yes, Coach!

1416
01:07:17,778 --> 01:07:20,111
In 1, 2, 3! Let's go!

1417
01:07:20,145 --> 01:07:22,678
Concentrate!

1418
01:07:22,678 --> 01:07:25,042
- Focus until the end!
- Yes!

1419
01:07:26,292 --> 01:07:28,611
- Stay focused until the game ends, Jin.
- Got it.

1420
01:07:28,612 --> 01:07:30,438
- Let's concentrate!
- Focus!

1421
01:07:30,439 --> 01:07:32,898
Min Ji, watch out for the short ones.

1422
01:07:32,924 --> 01:07:34,517
Reception.

1423
01:07:34,542 --> 01:07:37,652
(We must win this set.)

1424
01:07:38,001 --> 01:07:40,409
Hyeon Jeong's serve.

1425
01:07:40,753 --> 01:07:42,446
- Mine!
- Go!

1426
01:07:43,779 --> 01:07:45,461
(Ace Yun Ju's tip)

1427
01:07:46,130 --> 01:07:49,485
The defense was successful. A dink.

1428
01:07:51,376 --> 01:07:53,929
(The ball rises high, and here comes Jin!)

1429
01:07:55,352 --> 01:07:57,352
(Direct spike)

1430
01:07:58,032 --> 01:08:00,701
(Will she save this?)

1431
01:08:01,712 --> 01:08:03,874
It's a point.

1432
01:08:03,948 --> 01:08:06,475
- Alright.
- That was fortunate.

1433
01:08:06,584 --> 01:08:08,277
(Third Set, Pink Spiders 7
: Wonder Dogs 9)

1434
01:08:09,126 --> 01:08:11,875
(It was so close!)

1435
01:08:12,297 --> 01:08:14,890
(The match continues.)

1436
01:08:16,453 --> 01:08:18,353
Seung Ju spikes.

1437
01:08:19,136 --> 01:08:20,750
A success!

1438
01:08:22,913 --> 01:08:24,533
(Third Set, Pink Spiders 8
: Wonder Dogs 10)

1439
01:08:24,654 --> 01:08:28,538
(We must keep this momentum up.)

1440
01:08:29,506 --> 01:08:32,316
(Jin's serve)

1441
01:08:32,717 --> 01:08:33,434
It's out.

1442
01:08:33,443 --> 01:08:34,952
Hey!

1443
01:08:35,111 --> 01:08:36,437
(Out)

1444
01:08:40,149 --> 01:08:41,589
Jin!

1445
01:08:42,005 --> 01:08:44,291
Take your time before hitting.

1446
01:08:45,108 --> 01:08:48,882
An error never ends with just one point.

1447
01:08:49,358 --> 01:08:50,618
Min Ji, serve.

1448
01:08:50,653 --> 01:08:51,886
(Their error is our chance.)

1449
01:08:51,894 --> 01:08:53,135
Do it confidently.

1450
01:08:54,977 --> 01:08:56,597
(Min Ji serves,
following her team's pink flow)

1451
01:08:58,393 --> 01:08:59,643
(Good reception)

1452
01:09:01,690 --> 01:09:04,030
But it was a tip.

1453
01:09:04,259 --> 01:09:05,073
Nice!

1454
01:09:05,160 --> 01:09:06,773
(We scored!)

1455
01:09:07,997 --> 01:09:10,064
You need to cover! What were you doing?

1456
01:09:11,034 --> 01:09:13,401
Setter Jin is out of sync right now.

1457
01:09:14,048 --> 01:09:16,824
(We don't have time
for her to settle in now.)

1458
01:09:22,424 --> 01:09:23,652
(Dashing over)

1459
01:09:25,074 --> 01:09:29,476
They're replacing Jin with Sol.

1460
01:09:29,533 --> 01:09:32,919
The Wonder Dogs have
all three setters today.

1461
01:09:33,277 --> 01:09:35,971
(Third Set, Pink Spiders 10
: Wonder Dogs 11)

1462
01:09:36,581 --> 01:09:38,531
(We believe in Seung Ju's serve.)

1463
01:09:38,532 --> 01:09:39,733
Seung Ju serves.

1464
01:09:41,144 --> 01:09:43,911
- The net!
- Come now!

1465
01:09:44,431 --> 01:09:46,005
Yun Ju's spike!

1466
01:09:46,524 --> 01:09:48,722
Seung Ju sets it.

1467
01:09:48,772 --> 01:09:50,018
Sol!

1468
01:09:50,113 --> 01:09:51,500
(Sol's nice setup)

1469
01:09:53,282 --> 01:09:56,603
- Spike!
- It's out.

1470
01:09:57,603 --> 01:09:59,887
As soon as they change the setter...

1471
01:09:59,949 --> 01:10:02,682
She sets it right away,
and it leads to a point immediately.

1472
01:10:02,707 --> 01:10:03,763
(Powerful Enkhsoyol's spike)

1473
01:10:04,318 --> 01:10:07,026
(Score right after changing the setter)

1474
01:10:08,037 --> 01:10:11,182
(She signals to target Zone Four.)

1475
01:10:11,833 --> 01:10:13,993
(Targeted area)

1476
01:10:13,994 --> 01:10:15,476
(And Yun Ju,
a national team member, is there.)

1477
01:10:15,823 --> 01:10:17,554
Seung Ju's serve.

1478
01:10:19,207 --> 01:10:20,907
The reception was a bit off.

1479
01:10:21,250 --> 01:10:23,180
(A shaky ball)

1480
01:10:23,324 --> 01:10:24,424
Da Eun jumps.

1481
01:10:24,726 --> 01:10:27,173
We'll stop Da Eun with that.

1482
01:10:27,256 --> 01:10:29,810
Go for in between her and Min Ji.

1483
01:10:29,918 --> 01:10:31,745
Go for in between. Got it?

1484
01:10:32,946 --> 01:10:34,280
(Got it.)

1485
01:10:38,044 --> 01:10:40,686
(Point by blocking)

1486
01:10:41,829 --> 01:10:44,256
(She blocked in between them!)

1487
01:10:44,256 --> 01:10:45,732
Enkhsoyol!

1488
01:10:46,425 --> 01:10:49,976
(Enkhsoyol, you did a great job!)

1489
01:10:52,373 --> 01:10:54,300
("Things you can never give up:
your heart, money, the set")

1490
01:10:54,890 --> 01:10:59,320
The Wonder Dogs are ahead by one.

1491
01:10:59,360 --> 01:11:01,642
The Wonder Dogs widen the gap once again.

1492
01:11:02,383 --> 01:11:04,426
It's the Pink Spiders' chance ball.

1493
01:11:05,194 --> 01:11:06,545
Da Sol goes.

1494
01:11:07,297 --> 01:11:10,717
A tip! Seung Ju defends it successfully.

1495
01:11:11,066 --> 01:11:12,499
(Seung Ju sets an underhand toss!)

1496
01:11:12,594 --> 01:11:13,781
Come in!

1497
01:11:14,704 --> 01:11:17,196
(The small giant...)

1498
01:11:17,196 --> 01:11:18,972
(leaps up!)

1499
01:11:19,725 --> 01:11:21,701
Spike!

1500
01:11:21,844 --> 01:11:24,171
- Great!
- She did it!

1501
01:11:24,172 --> 01:11:27,460
(Third Set, Pink Spiders 11
: Wonder Dogs 14)

1502
01:11:28,009 --> 01:11:31,879
(She made that?)

1503
01:11:32,238 --> 01:11:34,974
(Clapping)

1504
01:11:35,235 --> 01:11:36,792
Song Hee, well done.

1505
01:11:38,453 --> 01:11:43,357
After the defense, the second setting was
precise, despite the difficult situation.

1506
01:11:43,399 --> 01:11:47,695
That's why Song Hee could spike
instead of just setting it up.

1507
01:11:47,696 --> 01:11:50,184
- She used to just set it.
- She did.

1508
01:11:52,008 --> 01:11:53,875
Tamira, go for in between.

1509
01:11:53,996 --> 01:11:56,096
Do it as you want.

1510
01:11:56,613 --> 01:11:58,606
Tamira, do whatever you like.

1511
01:11:59,556 --> 01:12:02,022
Tamira shows up at last.

1512
01:12:02,047 --> 01:12:03,137
Tamira is here.

1513
01:12:04,180 --> 01:12:05,700
She raises her right hand!

1514
01:12:06,054 --> 01:12:07,294
(Raising high)

1515
01:12:07,907 --> 01:12:11,542
(Here comes the spicy serve!)

1516
01:12:13,846 --> 01:12:16,035
(The reception crumbles.)

1517
01:12:17,591 --> 01:12:18,720
Good!

1518
01:12:19,095 --> 01:12:20,621
(No way!)

1519
01:12:24,798 --> 01:12:27,288
(That's the true taste
of Tamira's spicy serve!)

1520
01:12:27,497 --> 01:12:29,724
- Service point!
- Score!

1521
01:12:29,749 --> 01:12:31,839
Tamira!

1522
01:12:32,398 --> 01:12:34,186
(Everyone, put your hands up!)

1523
01:12:34,275 --> 01:12:35,267
(I'll copy her too!)

1524
01:12:36,232 --> 01:12:38,252
Tamira smiles as always today.

1525
01:12:38,318 --> 01:12:40,025
(Her miraculous serves continue.)

1526
01:12:40,643 --> 01:12:41,556
- Tamira!
- Tamira!

1527
01:12:42,147 --> 01:12:44,520
(Two thousand spectators chant her name.)

1528
01:12:46,794 --> 01:12:48,639
(She puts her arm up high in the air.)

1529
01:12:49,365 --> 01:12:52,268
(It's time to answer
the fans cheering for orange!)

1530
01:12:52,584 --> 01:12:53,519
(In between)

1531
01:12:53,520 --> 01:12:55,195
(Relax.)

1532
01:12:55,506 --> 01:12:57,289
(Got it.)

1533
01:12:58,642 --> 01:13:00,192
(Tamira's serve launches.)

1534
01:13:01,977 --> 01:13:05,606
(Yun Ju jumps up and spikes!)

1535
01:13:06,106 --> 01:13:08,325
(Captain Pyo's diving dig)

1536
01:13:09,198 --> 01:13:12,671
Spike! The defender's diving dig.

1537
01:13:12,672 --> 01:13:15,941
(The ball is once again set to Yun Ju!)

1538
01:13:16,533 --> 01:13:19,513
You figured Yun Ju out, right?
Her spike is always long.

1539
01:13:19,854 --> 01:13:21,205
(Okay.)

1540
01:13:21,413 --> 01:13:24,977
Don't put it up. You need
to block it off at the right timing.

1541
01:13:25,281 --> 01:13:27,845
(You remember, right?)

1542
01:13:30,996 --> 01:13:33,834
- Spike! It's blocked!
- Nice blocking!

1543
01:13:33,859 --> 01:13:36,030
Hyeon Jeong's block!

1544
01:13:36,737 --> 01:13:37,938
That's it.

1545
01:13:45,839 --> 01:13:49,448
(While everyone keeps
their eyes on the team,)

1546
01:13:50,149 --> 01:13:52,442
(the coach's strategy pushes
them ahead by five points.)

1547
01:13:53,829 --> 01:13:56,515
Good job. That was nice.

1548
01:13:58,127 --> 01:14:00,700
(The Wonder Dogs' players move
in sync like an orchestra.)

1549
01:14:01,137 --> 01:14:06,653
If you ask me the Wonder Dogs' strength,
I'd say it's their serves and blocks.

1550
01:14:06,701 --> 01:14:10,104
As Tamira joined, they scored with serves,
and now they're scoring with blocks too.

1551
01:14:10,105 --> 01:14:12,518
- There haven't been many blocking points.
- Right.

1552
01:14:12,670 --> 01:14:15,859
(Teamwork)

1553
01:14:15,957 --> 01:14:18,664
What if we win 3 to 0?

1554
01:14:18,828 --> 01:14:20,898
Don't get ahead of yourself and jinx it.

1555
01:14:20,899 --> 01:14:22,091
(Lips shut tight)

1556
01:14:22,133 --> 01:14:23,642
(They can't hide their joy.)

1557
01:14:24,335 --> 01:14:26,579
(Second technical timeout)

1558
01:14:26,628 --> 01:14:28,197
Nice job.

1559
01:14:28,314 --> 01:14:29,873
Tamira, nice serve.

1560
01:14:31,434 --> 01:14:33,232
I like the rhythm right now.

1561
01:14:33,282 --> 01:14:34,975
The bound is good. Keep this tempo up.

1562
01:14:34,979 --> 01:14:36,563
Don't let it go too far right.

1563
01:14:36,622 --> 01:14:37,873
Talk to each other.

1564
01:14:38,092 --> 01:14:39,850
Let's turn it around!

1565
01:14:39,884 --> 01:14:42,669
- Yun Ju, hit it more softly.
- Okay.

1566
01:14:42,730 --> 01:14:45,371
Or you can try again after rebounding.

1567
01:14:45,681 --> 01:14:47,428
Don't position for the ball to fly.

1568
01:14:47,462 --> 01:14:49,226
- Not too far. If so, they'll hit it.
- Yes, Coach.

1569
01:14:49,227 --> 01:14:50,424
So move more inward.

1570
01:14:50,479 --> 01:14:53,272
Let's make a side out!

1571
01:14:56,058 --> 01:14:59,703
(The Pink Spiders are trying
to turn the tables.)

1572
01:14:59,704 --> 01:15:01,669
Enkhsoyol, you're doing great.

1573
01:15:01,716 --> 01:15:04,303
(The Wonder Dogs are trying
to keep the momentum.)

1574
01:15:05,820 --> 01:15:07,146
It's 16 to 11.

1575
01:15:07,209 --> 01:15:09,489
The game resumes with Tamira's serve.

1576
01:15:11,787 --> 01:15:13,387
Get it!

1577
01:15:13,441 --> 01:15:15,281
- Good.
- Cover it!

1578
01:15:15,778 --> 01:15:17,444
Yun Ju.

1579
01:15:18,034 --> 01:15:19,589
The Wonder Dogs defend it.

1580
01:15:20,266 --> 01:15:22,335
(Here's a chance!)

1581
01:15:22,882 --> 01:15:24,970
(Now is the time!)

1582
01:15:29,892 --> 01:15:32,920
(But it was blocked.)

1583
01:15:32,921 --> 01:15:34,801
- My mistake.
- Let's try again.

1584
01:15:34,957 --> 01:15:37,237
The serve and defense were both good.

1585
01:15:37,273 --> 01:15:42,348
But Ji Su, the opponent,
had read through the move already.

1586
01:15:42,404 --> 01:15:43,424
(Ji Su's blocking)

1587
01:15:44,205 --> 01:15:45,378
Enkhsoyol!

1588
01:15:45,424 --> 01:15:46,642
(Don't spike it down!)

1589
01:15:46,674 --> 01:15:47,868
(Go long!)

1590
01:15:48,027 --> 01:15:49,822
- They'll come to block.
- Okay.

1591
01:15:52,231 --> 01:15:54,158
(Nodding)

1592
01:15:54,159 --> 01:15:55,635
(Peeking)

1593
01:15:57,479 --> 01:16:00,667
Da Sol, don't follow her around.

1594
01:16:00,717 --> 01:16:04,176
Coach Dae Kyung replaces
Da Sol with Ji Yun here.

1595
01:16:05,412 --> 01:16:07,229
We're repositioning in the third set.

1596
01:16:07,230 --> 01:16:08,547
(Before the third set began...)

1597
01:16:08,756 --> 01:16:12,025
Ji Yun and Hye Jin,
get ready to substitute in.

1598
01:16:12,862 --> 01:16:16,772
(They warmed up in advance.)

1599
01:16:17,815 --> 01:16:20,425
(As Ji Yun,
a national team member, subs in,)

1600
01:16:20,926 --> 01:16:23,996
(The Pink Spiders reinforce their attack!)

1601
01:16:24,429 --> 01:16:28,042
Since Ji Yun is on the national team,

1602
01:16:28,043 --> 01:16:30,344
the Wonder Dogs must keep their guard up.

1603
01:16:30,895 --> 01:16:33,514
(Da Eun's serve)

1604
01:16:34,757 --> 01:16:35,575
My ball!

1605
01:16:35,575 --> 01:16:37,108
Hye In.

1606
01:16:37,133 --> 01:16:39,280
- Sol.
- It was too low.

1607
01:16:42,047 --> 01:16:44,247
The defense was made on the left.

1608
01:16:45,117 --> 01:16:46,335
Ji Yun!

1609
01:16:46,594 --> 01:16:49,613
(Empty spot)

1610
01:16:52,041 --> 01:16:54,718
- Ji Yun scores.
- Well done.

1611
01:16:56,300 --> 01:17:00,548
(The Pink Spiders successfully score
two points in a row.)

1612
01:17:02,284 --> 01:17:03,986
(The match continues.)

1613
01:17:03,986 --> 01:17:06,980
Yun Ju's reception. She sets it. Spike!

1614
01:17:07,456 --> 01:17:09,860
(Did we defend it this time?)

1615
01:17:12,561 --> 01:17:14,062
Sol!

1616
01:17:15,839 --> 01:17:17,559
(So close!)

1617
01:17:19,035 --> 01:17:20,385
Ji Su blocks.

1618
01:17:20,455 --> 01:17:22,386
It's stopped again!

1619
01:17:22,411 --> 01:17:25,215
(Third set, Pink Spiders 14
: Wonder Dogs 17)

1620
01:17:25,654 --> 01:17:26,843
- Run!
- Sol.

1621
01:17:26,868 --> 01:17:29,375
(The momentum has completely shifted.)

1622
01:17:31,108 --> 01:17:33,148
- Oh!
- It is blocked!

1623
01:17:33,482 --> 01:17:36,449
Now Ji Yun is starting to find her rhythm.

1624
01:17:36,458 --> 01:17:39,112
The Pink Spiders' offense is
picking up steam.

1625
01:17:39,139 --> 01:17:39,889
It is.

1626
01:17:41,539 --> 01:17:44,618
(Breaking through Enkhsoyol's
strong defense is...)

1627
01:17:46,611 --> 01:17:49,943
(Power Ji Yun's double power!)

1628
01:17:51,842 --> 01:17:53,936
It's 15 to 18, a three-point difference.

1629
01:17:55,663 --> 01:17:56,939
Chae Rim!

1630
01:17:56,964 --> 01:17:57,949
(You're going in.)

1631
01:17:58,219 --> 01:17:58,839
Good luck!

1632
01:17:58,864 --> 01:18:02,120
Enkhsoyol steps out,
and Chae Rim steps in.

1633
01:18:03,105 --> 01:18:05,806
We're doing great! Let's go!

1634
01:18:05,831 --> 01:18:07,966
(Coach Kim's substitution
to counterattack Power Ji Yun)

1635
01:18:09,368 --> 01:18:12,029
(Let's go, Chae Rim!)

1636
01:18:12,389 --> 01:18:13,789
Clap, everyone!

1637
01:18:13,849 --> 01:18:15,366
- Baek Chae Rim!
- Baek Chae Rim!

1638
01:18:15,661 --> 01:18:18,369
(Chae Rim serving)

1639
01:18:18,849 --> 01:18:20,149
(Glancing)

1640
01:18:20,755 --> 01:18:22,368
(Assigning target service to Zone Four)

1641
01:18:23,297 --> 01:18:25,245
(Got it.)

1642
01:18:27,059 --> 01:18:28,972
- Chae Rim's service.
- Zone Four! Great!

1643
01:18:28,997 --> 01:18:30,470
- Cover it!
- I got it.

1644
01:18:30,508 --> 01:18:32,611
- Park Min Ji receives it.
- Cover it!

1645
01:18:35,061 --> 01:18:37,813
- Ji Yun spikes from the right!
- Nice one.

1646
01:18:38,666 --> 01:18:40,407
Ji Yun is bringing her A-game right now.

1647
01:18:40,432 --> 01:18:41,542
One more, okay?

1648
01:18:41,974 --> 01:18:43,786
Their spirits are dropping.

1649
01:18:45,172 --> 01:18:47,736
(We can't afford to allow
any points anymore.)

1650
01:18:47,763 --> 01:18:49,083
Let's get it together!

1651
01:18:49,811 --> 01:18:51,264
Give it your best, guys!

1652
01:18:51,289 --> 01:18:52,575
Ji Su serving.

1653
01:18:54,272 --> 01:18:57,326
- It's going to be a fast one!
- We need to get ready for it.

1654
01:18:57,811 --> 01:18:59,191
Watch the ball.

1655
01:19:02,868 --> 01:19:04,849
The set is a bit shaky.

1656
01:19:05,401 --> 01:19:07,543
Where on earth was that set going?

1657
01:19:09,846 --> 01:19:10,980
Seung Ju.

1658
01:19:12,114 --> 01:19:13,793
Yun Ju on defense.

1659
01:19:13,818 --> 01:19:14,984
- Hit it!
- Back-row attack.

1660
01:19:15,129 --> 01:19:16,452
A tip!

1661
01:19:16,970 --> 01:19:19,216
(Did they block it?)

1662
01:19:19,641 --> 01:19:21,991
A back-row tip. It gets blocked.

1663
01:19:22,717 --> 01:19:24,161
(The ball came over awkwardly.)

1664
01:19:24,186 --> 01:19:25,073
Run!

1665
01:19:26,501 --> 01:19:28,473
(The set is too short.)

1666
01:19:28,498 --> 01:19:29,999
Keep it alive!

1667
01:19:30,457 --> 01:19:31,733
What are you doing?

1668
01:19:32,232 --> 01:19:34,503
- Come on!
- What are you doing?

1669
01:19:37,415 --> 01:19:38,701
What the heck are they doing?

1670
01:19:38,726 --> 01:19:39,516
Jin!

1671
01:19:42,327 --> 01:19:43,082
Zone Three?

1672
01:19:43,107 --> 01:19:46,401
The setter looks rattled,
so Coach Kim calls for an immediate sub.

1673
01:19:46,426 --> 01:19:47,282
Exactly.

1674
01:19:47,414 --> 01:19:50,821
It's great
when the starting setter is stable,

1675
01:19:50,897 --> 01:19:53,473
but the setter on the bench gets
to watch from the sidelines,

1676
01:19:53,498 --> 01:19:56,425
giving her a better read
on the game's flow than the one playing.

1677
01:19:57,710 --> 01:20:00,238
(Resuming to Ji Su's serve)

1678
01:20:02,047 --> 01:20:02,656
Mine.

1679
01:20:02,680 --> 01:20:04,400
- Jin!
- Let's go!

1680
01:20:05,803 --> 01:20:06,669
Jin!

1681
01:20:06,696 --> 01:20:08,026
(Here's our chance!)

1682
01:20:08,051 --> 01:20:09,553
- Jin!
- Let's go!

1683
01:20:09,578 --> 01:20:11,674
Let's go!

1684
01:20:11,699 --> 01:20:12,741
Seung Ju!

1685
01:20:14,671 --> 01:20:15,978
The Pink Spiders save it.

1686
01:20:17,033 --> 01:20:18,400
Soft tip?

1687
01:20:19,985 --> 01:20:22,111
- Soft tip? It's still alive!
- It is!

1688
01:20:22,934 --> 01:20:25,387
Hye In throws herself for the save!

1689
01:20:26,437 --> 01:20:28,257
- We have to pass it over!
- We do!

1690
01:20:28,476 --> 01:20:29,856
It's on the other side now.

1691
01:20:29,881 --> 01:20:30,869
(Neither side is backing down.)

1692
01:20:32,178 --> 01:20:34,797
They save the tip.
Where will Jin go with it?

1693
01:20:34,822 --> 01:20:36,922
(To Captain Pyo again)

1694
01:20:37,278 --> 01:20:38,800
Seung Ju!

1695
01:20:38,917 --> 01:20:40,205
Ji Su receives it.

1696
01:20:40,294 --> 01:20:41,747
Keep it open!

1697
01:20:42,671 --> 01:20:45,126
(A high ball to Ji Yun)

1698
01:20:46,336 --> 01:20:50,547
(Power Ji Yun's attack is coming!)

1699
01:20:52,689 --> 01:20:54,316
Ji Yun spikes!

1700
01:20:55,945 --> 01:20:57,720
They couldn't dig that one.

1701
01:20:57,745 --> 01:20:58,974
(Another point lost)

1702
01:21:00,482 --> 01:21:02,768
Why did you run there?
That was Song Hee's ball.

1703
01:21:04,124 --> 01:21:07,797
The Pink Spiders are turning
the match around, led by Ji Yun.

1704
01:21:07,822 --> 01:21:09,310
(Third set, Pink Spiders 19
: Wonder Dogs 18)

1705
01:21:09,668 --> 01:21:13,097
Now it's 18 to 19.
We have to catch up right now.

1706
01:21:16,949 --> 01:21:18,621
(Nice receive)

1707
01:21:20,212 --> 01:21:21,243
Quick open.

1708
01:21:21,777 --> 01:21:22,945
Defended well.

1709
01:21:25,264 --> 01:21:26,381
Spike from the right!

1710
01:21:26,763 --> 01:21:27,951
(Ball rebounds high.)

1711
01:21:27,975 --> 01:21:28,851
They need to save it!

1712
01:21:28,876 --> 01:21:29,985
Jin!

1713
01:21:31,372 --> 01:21:33,021
Jin sprints and saves it!

1714
01:21:33,534 --> 01:21:35,601
Hye In with the bump set!

1715
01:21:35,669 --> 01:21:37,742
Seung Ju is reaching out!

1716
01:21:39,605 --> 01:21:41,058
Hye Jin digs it and steps out!

1717
01:21:46,013 --> 01:21:46,835
Hey!

1718
01:21:46,860 --> 01:21:48,070
The ball dropped!

1719
01:21:50,774 --> 01:21:52,441
Point for Wonder Dogs!

1720
01:21:52,466 --> 01:21:53,759
(Finally regaining the flow)

1721
01:21:54,344 --> 01:21:56,797
The score is tied at 19.

1722
01:21:57,492 --> 01:21:59,442
(After five long rallies)

1723
01:22:00,329 --> 01:22:02,217
Finally, they stop the bleeding.

1724
01:22:05,942 --> 01:22:07,189
Jin!

1725
01:22:08,617 --> 01:22:10,923
You're forcing it on Seung Ju too much.

1726
01:22:10,948 --> 01:22:12,561
Use your other options.

1727
01:22:14,463 --> 01:22:16,614
(Yeon Koung looks worried about Seung Ju.)

1728
01:22:17,857 --> 01:22:21,451
(In the previous match,)

1729
01:22:22,267 --> 01:22:24,276
(Seung Ju collapsed.)

1730
01:22:25,865 --> 01:22:29,052
(Coach Kim realized Seung Ju is drained.)

1731
01:22:30,787 --> 01:22:34,392
The pressure of the score is
definitely weighing on them.

1732
01:22:34,417 --> 01:22:35,719
Yes, it is.

1733
01:22:36,474 --> 01:22:38,448
They look like they're running on fumes.

1734
01:22:38,473 --> 01:22:39,437
Let's go!

1735
01:22:39,462 --> 01:22:42,191
I am the captain of this team,

1736
01:22:42,216 --> 01:22:47,196
and I can't afford to falter on the court.

1737
01:22:51,036 --> 01:22:54,376
The Wonder Dogs are putting up a hell
of a fight against the champion.

1738
01:22:55,000 --> 01:22:57,406
We need to toughen up.

1739
01:22:57,874 --> 01:23:01,877
I know it's not easy,
but they have to pull through.

1740
01:23:02,619 --> 01:23:03,612
Serve!

1741
01:23:04,852 --> 01:23:07,896
(Hyeon Jeong serving)

1742
01:23:13,232 --> 01:23:14,623
Min Ju's soft tip.

1743
01:23:15,050 --> 01:23:16,558
- Jin!
- Young In.

1744
01:23:17,022 --> 01:23:17,594
Jin!

1745
01:23:17,619 --> 01:23:19,428
Too tight to the net!

1746
01:23:20,023 --> 01:23:21,129
It's too close.

1747
01:23:21,385 --> 01:23:22,875
The set is wobbly.

1748
01:23:23,522 --> 01:23:24,666
Another soft tip.

1749
01:23:25,804 --> 01:23:27,636
Their play is getting messy.

1750
01:23:28,619 --> 01:23:30,005
Watch the tips!

1751
01:23:30,631 --> 01:23:32,277
(Ji Yun looking for an opening)

1752
01:23:32,537 --> 01:23:34,402
They should get it together
and strike again!

1753
01:23:34,434 --> 01:23:35,687
(But the set isn't steady again.)

1754
01:23:36,037 --> 01:23:37,990
(Captain Pyo)

1755
01:23:38,662 --> 01:23:40,949
Seung Ju spikes!

1756
01:23:41,439 --> 01:23:43,079
- It's out!
- And what's the call?

1757
01:23:44,498 --> 01:23:47,066
(Point for the Wonder Dogs)

1758
01:23:47,287 --> 01:23:49,491
Block-out! Point off the block!

1759
01:23:51,001 --> 01:23:53,295
The Wonder Dogs turn the tables again.

1760
01:23:53,320 --> 01:23:55,573
(The lead has flipped!)

1761
01:23:57,601 --> 01:24:00,761
With the sets wavering
and tips getting blocked,

1762
01:24:02,455 --> 01:24:06,375
Seung Ju adjusted her attack
and converted it into a point.

1763
01:24:06,400 --> 01:24:08,047
(Captain Pyo turned the table.)

1764
01:24:08,495 --> 01:24:13,515
Those were tough balls,
but Seung Ju handled them brilliantly.

1765
01:24:14,171 --> 01:24:15,760
(Riding the momentum)

1766
01:24:15,785 --> 01:24:16,652
Serve!

1767
01:24:16,760 --> 01:24:19,267
(Hyeon Jeong's serve)

1768
01:24:21,897 --> 01:24:23,592
(Where's the set going?)

1769
01:24:23,617 --> 01:24:24,826
Hye Jin, go!

1770
01:24:27,132 --> 01:24:28,697
Back set!

1771
01:24:29,761 --> 01:24:30,406
(Scrambling)

1772
01:24:30,431 --> 01:24:31,733
They're chasing it down.

1773
01:24:33,448 --> 01:24:36,429
(Ji Yun's surprise attack)

1774
01:24:36,975 --> 01:24:38,673
Sneak attack by Ji Yun!

1775
01:24:39,193 --> 01:24:41,249
(Third set, Pink Spiders 20
: Wonder Dogs 20)

1776
01:24:43,360 --> 01:24:45,814
Ace Ji Yun scores again to tie it up.

1777
01:24:49,780 --> 01:24:51,260
(The Wonder Dogs have
the veteran Captain Pyo,)

1778
01:24:52,473 --> 01:24:54,413
(but the opponent has
the powerhouse, Ji Yun.)

1779
01:24:55,088 --> 01:24:56,874
(To lead their team to victory,)

1780
01:24:57,473 --> 01:24:59,626
(the aces face off,
neither giving an inch.)

1781
01:24:59,651 --> 01:25:02,046
(We have to take the lead!)

1782
01:25:02,421 --> 01:25:04,366
Ji Yun is serving.

1783
01:25:06,478 --> 01:25:07,560
Seung Ju.

1784
01:25:07,587 --> 01:25:08,504
Jin.

1785
01:25:09,106 --> 01:25:11,272
Hitting it in rhythm.

1786
01:25:12,941 --> 01:25:15,010
Ji Yun can't dig it.

1787
01:25:16,900 --> 01:25:18,683
Wonder Dogs score!

1788
01:25:18,707 --> 01:25:23,252
The captain is leaving it all
on the floor.

1789
01:25:26,467 --> 01:25:28,683
Nice save with a quick backstep.

1790
01:25:29,016 --> 01:25:30,759
It's Seung Ju, again!

1791
01:25:30,869 --> 01:25:32,294
- Look up!
- Hit it!

1792
01:25:35,658 --> 01:25:37,065
Blocked this time.

1793
01:25:38,534 --> 01:25:40,135
Okay!

1794
01:25:43,666 --> 01:25:44,886
Sorry.

1795
01:25:45,680 --> 01:25:47,471
(The moment you let your guard down,)

1796
01:25:47,496 --> 01:25:49,490
(you lose a point.)

1797
01:25:49,514 --> 01:25:51,513
The battle is fierce.

1798
01:25:52,067 --> 01:25:54,382
They need to pull ahead now.

1799
01:25:55,029 --> 01:25:56,505
It's 23 to 22.

1800
01:25:56,552 --> 01:25:59,118
(Pink Spiders' tactical timeout)

1801
01:25:59,965 --> 01:26:02,391
Everyone, bring it in. Closer.

1802
01:26:02,957 --> 01:26:06,242
We're serving to Zone Four.

1803
01:26:06,266 --> 01:26:08,133
That leaves two attackers.

1804
01:26:08,158 --> 01:26:10,671
You get ready to receive,
and you step up in advance.

1805
01:26:10,696 --> 01:26:12,436
They might drop it short. Read the ball.

1806
01:26:12,467 --> 01:26:15,420
Got it? Stay compact and cover each other.

1807
01:26:15,696 --> 01:26:17,239
Jump in early for the quick ones.

1808
01:26:17,670 --> 01:26:20,929
(While Wonder Dogs are busy strategizing,)

1809
01:26:21,549 --> 01:26:23,048
Watch out for the short serves.

1810
01:26:23,073 --> 01:26:24,652
Don't overcomplicate it.
It's okay, just hit it.

1811
01:26:24,677 --> 01:26:25,898
Others will cover it.

1812
01:26:25,923 --> 01:26:28,984
Stay close on the left, and run the "Sha."

1813
01:26:29,425 --> 01:26:31,265
- Okay.
- You can do the "Sha," right, Ji Yun?

1814
01:26:33,065 --> 01:26:34,517
(The play that scored
for the Pink Spiders earlier)

1815
01:26:35,587 --> 01:26:38,474
(A surprise back-toss connecting
to Ji Yun's attack)

1816
01:26:38,499 --> 01:26:41,307
(The name of the play is "Sha.")

1817
01:26:41,772 --> 01:26:43,298
You can do the "Sha," right, Ji Yun?

1818
01:26:43,892 --> 01:26:45,234
Just rip it when you see it.

1819
01:26:45,259 --> 01:26:48,203
Stay close on the left, and run the "Sha."

1820
01:26:48,718 --> 01:26:50,874
- And stay close to cover.
- Okay.

1821
01:26:50,899 --> 01:26:51,901
(Coach Kim's prediction is off.)

1822
01:26:51,926 --> 01:26:53,981
- Just hit long between five and six.
- Okay.

1823
01:26:55,107 --> 01:26:58,547
When it feels a bit high,
just hit it straight.

1824
01:26:58,572 --> 01:27:01,650
- Got it?
- Yes. Go, Wonder Dogs!

1825
01:27:02,874 --> 01:27:05,387
(Returning to the court,
unaware of the wrong tactic)

1826
01:27:05,412 --> 01:27:07,322
Receive it well.

1827
01:27:08,126 --> 01:27:10,992
Two points away from victory.

1828
01:27:11,017 --> 01:27:13,075
(The coaches' moves...)

1829
01:27:13,781 --> 01:27:16,165
(might lead to unexpected results.)

1830
01:27:17,359 --> 01:27:18,333
Go!

1831
01:27:22,615 --> 01:27:23,679
(Well-targeted service)

1832
01:27:23,703 --> 01:27:24,703
It's placed precisely.

1833
01:27:25,578 --> 01:27:27,613
(Preparing for a left attack as planned)

1834
01:27:27,821 --> 01:27:31,959
(But the toss goes to the right.)

1835
01:27:36,263 --> 01:27:37,998
(As they were waiting for a left attack,)

1836
01:27:38,277 --> 01:27:39,809
(the right side is open wide.)

1837
01:27:41,047 --> 01:27:42,899
Ji Yun's sudden attack!

1838
01:27:42,924 --> 01:27:44,375
(We're the ones to take the point!)

1839
01:27:44,966 --> 01:27:46,961
- She defended it!
- Nice!

1840
01:27:47,269 --> 01:27:48,196
Nice defense.

1841
01:27:49,131 --> 01:27:50,866
(And Su Bin keeps the ball alive.)

1842
01:27:51,397 --> 01:27:52,934
The ball is sent over the net.

1843
01:27:54,507 --> 01:27:55,575
A calm toss.

1844
01:27:56,542 --> 01:27:57,225
(Off-beat)

1845
01:27:57,250 --> 01:27:58,384
They weren't in sync.

1846
01:27:58,658 --> 01:28:00,927
And the chance goes to the Wonder Dogs.

1847
01:28:02,540 --> 01:28:04,345
They can't afford to miss the chance!

1848
01:28:05,991 --> 01:28:07,783
- Young In on the right side!
- Young In!

1849
01:28:11,296 --> 01:28:12,931
It's out.

1850
01:28:13,711 --> 01:28:15,290
Goodness!

1851
01:28:16,901 --> 01:28:20,938
I understand the desire
to score was so strong,

1852
01:28:20,938 --> 01:28:24,241
she wanted to take the point herself,

1853
01:28:24,509 --> 01:28:26,544
but she put in too much power.

1854
01:28:27,532 --> 01:28:28,566
Young In!

1855
01:28:28,992 --> 01:28:30,093
It's all right.

1856
01:28:33,243 --> 01:28:35,857
(The game is back to square one.)

1857
01:28:37,841 --> 01:28:39,709
When the free ball comes,
go with a back B.

1858
01:28:40,411 --> 01:28:41,411
Hey!

1859
01:28:41,592 --> 01:28:42,960
- "Sha" to back B.
- Got it.

1860
01:28:45,730 --> 01:28:47,632
The score is 23 to 23.

1861
01:28:51,299 --> 01:28:52,742
(A c-quick sign to Chae Rim)

1862
01:28:52,767 --> 01:28:53,828
Let's go!

1863
01:28:57,939 --> 01:29:00,875
(Both teams are just two points away
from a set victory.)

1864
01:29:00,875 --> 01:29:01,843
(Exhaling)

1865
01:29:04,542 --> 01:29:05,443
Hye In.

1866
01:29:05,468 --> 01:29:06,641
Cover the attack!

1867
01:29:08,338 --> 01:29:09,172
Jin.

1868
01:29:10,240 --> 01:29:11,875
Chae Rim, you go!

1869
01:29:13,576 --> 01:29:14,443
Are you crazy?

1870
01:29:15,138 --> 01:29:16,351
Have you lost your mind?

1871
01:29:16,531 --> 01:29:18,917
(A chance to make up for her mistake)

1872
01:29:19,256 --> 01:29:21,904
(The rookie coach gives her a chance
to redeem herself.)

1873
01:29:22,848 --> 01:29:24,783
(Zone Six is open.)

1874
01:29:27,449 --> 01:29:29,418
She pushed it into Zone Six for a point!

1875
01:29:29,458 --> 01:29:30,966
- Chae Rim's point!
- Great!

1876
01:29:34,030 --> 01:29:35,770
Thank you!

1877
01:29:36,338 --> 01:29:38,774
(Overcoming the hurdles one by one)

1878
01:29:38,774 --> 01:29:40,375
Please!

1879
01:29:41,110 --> 01:29:44,013
(A precious point)

1880
01:29:45,178 --> 01:29:46,072
(Floor slap)

1881
01:29:47,261 --> 01:29:49,997
(The Wonder Dogs reclaim the lead.)

1882
01:29:50,871 --> 01:29:53,507
(I trusted you, Chae Rim!)

1883
01:29:53,842 --> 01:29:59,281
That point by Chae Rim was
absolutely crucial.

1884
01:29:59,306 --> 01:30:00,237
Exactly!

1885
01:30:00,469 --> 01:30:01,737
That was a massive play.

1886
01:30:01,737 --> 01:30:03,834
(Only one point to the victory)

1887
01:30:05,441 --> 01:30:06,802
I'm confident we can win.

1888
01:30:07,422 --> 01:30:08,797
Watch them closing in!

1889
01:30:09,464 --> 01:30:10,765
Let's go!

1890
01:30:11,146 --> 01:30:14,015
We've come this far,
I know we can do this.

1891
01:30:14,969 --> 01:30:15,937
We're going to win.

1892
01:30:16,991 --> 01:30:19,256
Just one point, please.

1893
01:30:22,243 --> 01:30:24,946
Wonder Dogs are at match point.

1894
01:30:24,971 --> 01:30:27,365
(Wonder Dogs' match point)

1895
01:30:29,114 --> 01:30:31,168
(Coach Kim Dae Kyung stays calm.)

1896
01:30:31,193 --> 01:30:32,361
Run the same play.

1897
01:30:32,361 --> 01:30:34,439
(Same play. The "Sha")

1898
01:30:35,303 --> 01:30:37,972
(We'll beat you with "Sha.")

1899
01:30:39,780 --> 01:30:41,382
Myoung Hwa to serve.

1900
01:30:42,472 --> 01:30:44,574
(Aim for Zone Three.)

1901
01:30:44,646 --> 01:30:45,914
(Okay, Coach.)

1902
01:30:53,086 --> 01:30:54,252
(Unsteady receive near Zone 3)

1903
01:30:54,276 --> 01:30:55,617
Their reception is Shaky!

1904
01:30:57,700 --> 01:30:59,468
(Back set from Hye Jin)

1905
01:30:59,942 --> 01:31:01,189
Same play!

1906
01:31:03,706 --> 01:31:04,807
No blockers!

1907
01:31:05,841 --> 01:31:06,775
Nobody's there!

1908
01:31:07,683 --> 01:31:09,084
It's wide open!

1909
01:31:09,785 --> 01:31:10,619
Nobody's there!

1910
01:31:10,948 --> 01:31:12,015
Bring it!

1911
01:31:12,015 --> 01:31:13,517
Ji Yun skies for it!

1912
01:31:14,954 --> 01:31:17,452
(No blockers!)

1913
01:31:25,632 --> 01:31:27,734
(Wait.)

1914
01:31:27,734 --> 01:31:30,812
(Out)

1915
01:31:37,661 --> 01:31:38,762
Out!

1916
01:31:40,506 --> 01:31:43,576
(Third set, Pink Spiders 23
: Wonder Dogs 25)

1917
01:31:45,818 --> 01:31:47,420
Yes!

1918
01:31:48,588 --> 01:31:52,609
(The underdogs stage an upset!)

1919
01:31:53,252 --> 01:31:57,289
- The call is out!
- It's out!

1920
01:32:02,337 --> 01:32:04,239
The match is over!

1921
01:32:04,573 --> 01:32:06,708
A set score of 3 to 0!

1922
01:32:07,557 --> 01:32:11,257
(Wonder Dogs win via shutout)

1923
01:32:14,497 --> 01:32:19,044
(Now the Wonder Dogs can finally smile.)

1924
01:32:20,703 --> 01:32:24,494
(We won the final match!)

1925
01:32:39,735 --> 01:32:41,136
(Smiles spreading across the arena)

1926
01:32:41,161 --> 01:32:42,562
(Legend Youn Koung,
From Underdogs to Wonder Dogs!)

1927
01:32:45,941 --> 01:32:48,830
- You worked so hard.
- Good job, everyone.

1928
01:32:50,392 --> 01:32:51,733
Why are you crying?

1929
01:33:01,544 --> 01:33:04,615
(The foolish world may not see you)

1930
01:33:05,761 --> 01:33:08,998
(It cannot see the "you"
hidden inside the cocoon)

1931
01:33:09,711 --> 01:33:13,339
(But I know, and I can see)

1932
01:33:14,482 --> 01:33:17,994
(Your wings, shining brilliantly)

1933
01:33:18,561 --> 01:33:19,996
(Hyeon Jeong and Seung Ju,
You Are the Best!)

1934
01:33:19,996 --> 01:33:21,798
(Song Hee Is Awesome!)

1935
01:33:22,457 --> 01:33:26,594
The Wonder Dogs' final match...

1936
01:33:26,695 --> 01:33:29,831
against the Pink Spiders ends in victory!

1937
01:33:31,193 --> 01:33:35,642
(Rise and soar over the world!)

1938
01:34:10,872 --> 01:34:12,314
Good job.

1939
01:34:16,011 --> 01:34:19,981
Fourteen players, each carrying
their own scars and frustrations,

1940
01:34:20,415 --> 01:34:23,351
all started clearly as underdogs.

1941
01:34:24,080 --> 01:34:27,140
(The journey began two months ago.)

1942
01:34:27,473 --> 01:34:30,709
(Some held onto regrets.)

1943
01:34:30,710 --> 01:34:33,346
(Others held onto longing.)

1944
01:34:33,852 --> 01:34:38,023
(They were still lacking in so many ways.)

1945
01:34:39,011 --> 01:34:42,982
(Reality wasn't like a drama)

1946
01:34:44,524 --> 01:34:48,087
(Just humble cocoons)

1947
01:34:49,007 --> 01:34:50,175
A quick attack!

1948
01:34:50,284 --> 01:34:51,374
(Struggling...)

1949
01:34:51,399 --> 01:34:53,188
I want to go home!

1950
01:34:53,865 --> 01:34:56,701
(with all your might!)

1951
01:34:56,988 --> 01:34:58,193
Bring it on!

1952
01:34:59,566 --> 01:35:02,973
(Volleyball is a sport
where you must always look up.)

1953
01:35:04,316 --> 01:35:07,992
(Flap your wings without giving up.)

1954
01:35:09,448 --> 01:35:13,665
(Aim not just for a happy ending,
but the best ending possible.)

1955
01:35:14,419 --> 01:35:17,956
Erasing the label of "underdog"
one by one,

1956
01:35:18,218 --> 01:35:21,221
and creating moments of awe and wonder,

1957
01:35:21,314 --> 01:35:24,117
they finally became the Wonder Dogs.

1958
01:35:24,785 --> 01:35:26,553
From underdogs to Wonder Dogs!

1959
01:35:29,670 --> 01:35:32,573
We are much stronger than people think.

1960
01:35:32,952 --> 01:35:35,755
I'm just glad we finished on a high note.

1961
01:35:36,797 --> 01:35:38,132
I was really moved.

1962
01:35:41,301 --> 01:35:42,202
Song Hee!

1963
01:35:42,963 --> 01:35:44,639
Great job!

1964
01:35:46,239 --> 01:35:49,075
Every single player contributed...

1965
01:35:49,242 --> 01:35:51,144
and everyone played their part perfectly.

1966
01:35:51,144 --> 01:35:53,279
Seung Kwan!

1967
01:35:53,747 --> 01:35:54,781
Who was that?

1968
01:35:54,781 --> 01:35:57,117
Guys, bring it in.

1969
01:36:00,487 --> 01:36:02,255
You should do this together.

1970
01:36:04,658 --> 01:36:06,094
- In 1, 2, 3!
- In 1, 2, 3!

1971
01:36:07,561 --> 01:36:08,629
- In 1, 2, 3!
- In 1, 2, 3!

1972
01:36:10,110 --> 01:36:11,399
- In 1, 2, 3!
- In 1, 2, 3!

1973
01:36:13,006 --> 01:36:14,641
It's too high!

1974
01:36:15,842 --> 01:36:18,211
I really felt like we became one team.

1975
01:36:18,645 --> 01:36:23,349
Our players have improved
way more than I expected,

1976
01:36:23,603 --> 01:36:27,982
and as a coach, I'm incredibly satisfied.

1977
01:36:28,694 --> 01:36:30,996
Honestly, seeing these results...

1978
01:36:31,698 --> 01:36:33,767
makes the loss to the Altos
sting even more.

1979
01:36:34,440 --> 01:36:36,809
(Her unstoppable competitive spirit)

1980
01:36:37,420 --> 01:36:39,889
(Greeting her juniors
from her former team)

1981
01:36:40,193 --> 01:36:42,862
Hey, what got into you guys?

1982
01:36:42,920 --> 01:36:44,432
Why are you guys so good?

1983
01:36:44,965 --> 01:36:46,566
What happened out there?

1984
01:36:46,566 --> 01:36:48,034
(She's a little sad.)

1985
01:36:48,299 --> 01:36:50,266
Ji Eun, tell me. What happened?

1986
01:36:50,267 --> 01:36:52,644
(Teasing her juniors out of affection)

1987
01:36:53,695 --> 01:36:55,830
(Unstoppable love for her juniors)

1988
01:36:55,855 --> 01:36:56,856
(Come on.)

1989
01:36:57,274 --> 01:36:59,046
Our final record...

1990
01:37:00,512 --> 01:37:01,741
five wins and two losses.

1991
01:37:01,766 --> 01:37:03,674
(Final record:
5 wins, 2 losses in 7 matches)

1992
01:37:04,247 --> 01:37:06,983
We made it!

1993
01:37:08,051 --> 01:37:09,019
We did it!

1994
01:37:09,520 --> 01:37:10,810
We have a gift for you.

1995
01:37:10,835 --> 01:37:12,226
- A gift?
- A gift?

1996
01:37:15,292 --> 01:37:17,031
Our names are on the plate.

1997
01:37:19,229 --> 01:37:21,398
Look, there are our names.

1998
01:37:21,398 --> 01:37:22,929
(Pilseung Wonder Dogs)

1999
01:37:22,954 --> 01:37:24,872
They made this after the game.

2000
01:37:25,735 --> 01:37:28,109
In 1, 2, 3.

2001
01:37:28,134 --> 01:37:31,840
(Taking a final photo before wrapping up)

2002
01:37:33,262 --> 01:37:34,883
Do you remember the tryouts?

2003
01:37:35,049 --> 01:37:36,082
Yes, I do.

2004
01:37:36,161 --> 01:37:37,451
You remember?

2005
01:37:37,654 --> 01:37:39,087
Of course. How could I forget?

2006
01:37:41,395 --> 01:37:43,595
Everyone looked so serious.

2007
01:37:43,595 --> 01:37:44,661
Look at their faces.

2008
01:37:44,661 --> 01:37:46,261
(Their awkward first meeting)

2009
01:37:46,261 --> 01:37:47,495
Is it that bad?

2010
01:37:48,828 --> 01:37:49,861
Hello.

2011
01:37:49,886 --> 01:37:51,743
(Staring intensely)

2012
01:37:52,529 --> 01:37:53,668
I remember that.

2013
01:37:54,761 --> 01:37:57,928
Coach probably doesn't remember me
from when I was little.

2014
01:37:59,502 --> 01:38:01,436
I'm Koo Hye In, ninth grade.

2015
01:38:01,461 --> 01:38:04,295
Koo Hye In will learn to play.

2016
01:38:04,295 --> 01:38:06,861
(A connection from seven years ago)

2017
01:38:06,886 --> 01:38:09,853
She's textbook when it comes to receiving.

2018
01:38:11,431 --> 01:38:13,564
Yes, that's me. Surprise.

2019
01:38:13,564 --> 01:38:15,164
(Hye In dreamed of becoming
Kim Yeon Koung.)

2020
01:38:15,164 --> 01:38:17,051
You'll be standing here
in ten years, right?

2021
01:38:17,076 --> 01:38:18,259
(Seven years later, she had drifted
from that dream.)

2022
01:38:18,764 --> 01:38:21,598
As a libero, I couldn't really show
what I was capable of.

2023
01:38:22,031 --> 01:38:25,564
I just wanted to be on the court,
so I applied.

2024
01:38:26,022 --> 01:38:28,690
(And with the Wonder Dogs,
she achieved...)

2025
01:38:28,715 --> 01:38:30,850
(her dream.)

2026
01:38:31,170 --> 01:38:33,238
When I'm a starter,
I get to play the whole match.

2027
01:38:33,263 --> 01:38:36,563
That's what my grandma loved most.

2028
01:38:37,537 --> 01:38:39,704
Thank you for coming. It's over now.

2029
01:38:39,704 --> 01:38:40,870
(Patting)

2030
01:38:42,210 --> 01:38:44,185
These moments felt like a dream.

2031
01:38:45,916 --> 01:38:47,716
(Sixth grade, twelve years ago)

2032
01:38:48,056 --> 01:38:50,589
I earn around 1,000 dollars a month.

2033
01:38:50,614 --> 01:38:53,980
That was when I first became a starter.

2034
01:38:54,149 --> 01:38:55,649
Koo Sol!

2035
01:38:56,683 --> 01:38:58,485
(A dream so intense it was dizzying)

2036
01:38:58,510 --> 01:38:59,767
Sol!

2037
01:38:59,950 --> 01:39:01,250
(Nice set.)

2038
01:39:02,254 --> 01:39:04,939
I was happy to be recognized.

2039
01:39:08,287 --> 01:39:12,787
I think I held onto my dream
just by looking up to her.

2040
01:39:13,087 --> 01:39:15,187
(Eighth grade, twelve years ago)

2041
01:39:15,293 --> 01:39:17,886
What would it feel like to be out there?

2042
01:39:17,887 --> 01:39:19,456
(Young In was curious
about the pro world.)

2043
01:39:19,481 --> 01:39:21,850
I want to go back to a pro team.

2044
01:39:22,126 --> 01:39:25,059
That's been my dream all along.
It feels unreal even now.

2045
01:39:25,920 --> 01:39:30,320
I don't know how longer I'll play.

2046
01:39:31,202 --> 01:39:35,203
I gained the confidence to start over.

2047
01:39:35,839 --> 01:39:37,006
Hit it!

2048
01:39:38,698 --> 01:39:39,865
Nice!

2049
01:39:40,106 --> 01:39:44,739
I felt a fire deep inside to do well.

2050
01:39:45,008 --> 01:39:48,308
For me, this will stay
as a beautiful memory forever...

2051
01:39:48,333 --> 01:39:50,617
because we ended on a high note.

2052
01:39:51,308 --> 01:39:54,209
My volleyball career might have had
a bad ending,

2053
01:39:54,234 --> 01:39:57,367
but thanks to the Wonder Dogs,
it feels like a good one now.

2054
01:39:57,392 --> 01:39:59,477
(Seung Ju and Su Bin kept dreaming,
even after retiring.)

2055
01:40:00,194 --> 01:40:02,694
I'm so glad to show
that I can play volleyball...

2056
01:40:02,719 --> 01:40:04,919
even if I'm short.

2057
01:40:06,048 --> 01:40:10,808
(Playing despite living
in a foreign country)

2058
01:40:10,833 --> 01:40:13,267
It felt like a dream.

2059
01:40:14,252 --> 01:40:17,645
A moment I'll never forget in my life.

2060
01:40:18,378 --> 01:40:19,845
It'll stay with me forever.

2061
01:40:21,906 --> 01:40:23,447
(A fiercely passionate and pure dream)

2062
01:40:23,907 --> 01:40:25,253
I'm just enjoying volleyball now.

2063
01:40:26,100 --> 01:40:29,267
I have no idea when I'll stop.

2064
01:40:29,726 --> 01:40:32,260
But this was a beautiful dream for me.

2065
01:40:33,608 --> 01:40:39,504
(Wonder Dogs was a beautiful dream.)

2066
01:40:40,211 --> 01:40:43,477
(And for this girl...)

2067
01:40:43,911 --> 01:40:45,777
(About 20 years later)

2068
01:40:46,144 --> 01:40:47,977
(Heungkuk Life Insurance Training Center)

2069
01:40:49,644 --> 01:40:52,144
(At the Pink Spiders' training ground,)

2070
01:40:52,611 --> 01:40:54,677
(Is that Lee Na Yeon?)

2071
01:40:55,009 --> 01:40:56,343
What happened?

2072
01:40:56,368 --> 01:40:58,168
(Lee Na Yeon Returns to Pro Volleyball,
Signs with Pink Spiders)

2073
01:40:58,862 --> 01:41:02,262
(Na Yeon becomes a pro player.)

2074
01:41:02,476 --> 01:41:07,576
Back when I had the pre-interview...

2075
01:41:08,229 --> 01:41:11,096
No way I'll go pro.

2076
01:41:11,121 --> 01:41:13,601
I don't think I can be a pro player.

2077
01:41:13,850 --> 01:41:16,683
- This is all I need now.
- The tryout?

2078
01:41:17,220 --> 01:41:20,797
(Then, starting with the Wonder Dogs...)

2079
01:41:20,966 --> 01:41:26,000
Pohang City Hall needed a setter,
so I decided to go.

2080
01:41:26,907 --> 01:41:31,300
(She got a chance as a setter
in the industrial league.)

2081
01:41:31,845 --> 01:41:35,389
They suggested I join the Pink Spiders.

2082
01:41:36,191 --> 01:41:41,057
I thought, "Sure. There's an offer,
I should at least take the test."

2083
01:41:41,491 --> 01:41:43,357
So I took it.

2084
01:41:44,846 --> 01:41:46,579
(In just a few months,)

2085
01:41:46,846 --> 01:41:51,013
I was living my life
thinking I'd played long enough.

2086
01:41:51,580 --> 01:41:55,913
I might have just kept living that way
if I hadn't joined this show.

2087
01:41:55,938 --> 01:41:57,705
(This wouldn't have happened
without the Wonder Dogs.)

2088
01:41:57,791 --> 01:42:00,410
(Also, in the industrial league
following the final match,)

2089
01:42:01,171 --> 01:42:03,749
(Hye In, the Guardian,
won the Libero Award.)

2090
01:42:04,271 --> 01:42:06,937
(Myoung Hwa, the Serving Queen,
won the Serve Award.)

2091
01:42:07,538 --> 01:42:10,594
(Chae Rim, the Ultimate Weapon,
won the Attacker Award.)

2092
01:42:11,197 --> 01:42:15,921
(The players grew
from "under" to "wonder.")

2093
01:42:16,914 --> 01:42:17,921
How should I explain it?

2094
01:42:17,946 --> 01:42:19,455
(What is Coach Kim to you?)

2095
01:42:20,247 --> 01:42:25,406
She's the person who led me
back to volleyball.

2096
01:42:26,101 --> 01:42:28,586
(A few days later)

2097
01:42:34,913 --> 01:42:36,547
(The rookie coach visits the MBC studio.)

2098
01:42:36,572 --> 01:42:37,838
You did a great job.

2099
01:42:38,267 --> 01:42:39,633
(Glaring)

2100
01:42:40,047 --> 01:42:41,947
Come here. Where have you been?

2101
01:42:41,972 --> 01:42:43,350
(Where is she, anyway?)

2102
01:42:44,167 --> 01:42:47,167
(The place where she started
as a rookie coach...)

2103
01:42:47,780 --> 01:42:51,022
(and where the Wonder Dogs' dreams began)

2104
01:42:51,115 --> 01:42:54,096
I remember when we first met
and filmed here.

2105
01:42:54,121 --> 01:42:55,803
Enough with the sentimental stuff.
Just film.

2106
01:42:57,181 --> 01:43:00,614
You became a head coach
for the first time,

2107
01:43:00,868 --> 01:43:04,001
- and you achieved incredible results.
- That's true.

2108
01:43:04,581 --> 01:43:06,348
Five wins out of seven matches.

2109
01:43:07,181 --> 01:43:08,115
Two losses.

2110
01:43:08,275 --> 01:43:10,741
(On top of that,
three were shutout victories.)

2111
01:43:10,894 --> 01:43:13,194
- It wasn't bad.
- A winning rate of 71.4 percent.

2112
01:43:13,332 --> 01:43:15,432
That's a record worthy of a champion team.

2113
01:43:15,467 --> 01:43:17,134
It's amazing, isn't it?

2114
01:43:17,834 --> 01:43:18,521
Quite.

2115
01:43:18,545 --> 01:43:20,701
But why did you call me here today?

2116
01:43:20,726 --> 01:43:25,460
We've been working to establish
the eighth pro club.

2117
01:43:26,393 --> 01:43:32,893
Our matches have generated a lot of buzz
in the volleyball world.

2118
01:43:33,000 --> 01:43:35,500
- A lot of important people were watching.
- Okay.

2119
01:43:35,525 --> 01:43:36,614
(What is he trying to say?)

2120
01:43:36,639 --> 01:43:38,383
About the eighth club...

2121
01:43:46,782 --> 01:43:50,228
(Kim Yeon Koung as Head Coach)

2122
01:43:50,574 --> 01:43:53,280
(Pyo Seung Ju, Enkhsoyol, Tamira)

2123
01:43:53,305 --> 01:43:55,687
(Back Chae Rim, Han Song Hee,
Yoon Young In)

2124
01:43:55,714 --> 01:43:58,381
(Lee Jin, Lee Na Yeon, Koo Sol)

2125
01:43:58,381 --> 01:44:01,149
(Kim Na Hee, Moon Myoung Hwa,
Kim Hyeon Jeong)

2126
01:44:01,174 --> 01:44:03,608
(Koo Hye In, Choi Su Bin)

2127
01:44:03,734 --> 01:44:05,830
(Commentators Lee Ho Geun and Lee Suk Ja)

2128
01:44:05,956 --> 01:44:08,958
(Managers Boo Seung Kwan and Lee Kyung Ha)

2129
01:44:08,983 --> 01:44:12,275
(Coaches Kim Tae Young, Lee Yeon Ju,
and Jeong Wu Seong)

2130
01:44:12,681 --> 01:44:14,681
(Performance analysts
Chae Sang Min and Nam Ye Rin)

2131
01:44:14,814 --> 01:44:16,940
(Trainers Lee Sang Hwa,
Jeong Jong Il, and Park Ye Jin)

2132
01:45:04,524 --> 01:45:06,590
(May "wonder" be with you
in your life too.)
